[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255","ref":{"name":"section"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"section","hasChildren":1,"tag":"h2"},"pos":"212","docId":"75","text":"TITLE 11: VEHICLES AND TRAFFIC","id":"ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/1588a26f-dd49-4acc-aa5c-238d214e9d0e","ref":{"parent":"ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"1588a26f-dd49-4acc-aa5c-238d214e9d0e","prev_id":null},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35","ref":{"parent":"ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":1,"tag":"h3"},"pos":"212-12","docId":"75","text":"CHAPTER 11.04: ABANDONED, WRECKED, INOPERATIVE VEHICLES","id":"a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/3dbf73b0-80c6-46e4-a2dc-1b6ae1437141","ref":{"parent":"a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-12-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003E* For statutory provisions regarding the abatement and removal of abandoned vehicles, see Veh. Code \u00a7 22650 et seq.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"3dbf73b0-80c6-46e4-a2dc-1b6ae1437141","prev_id":null},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/2cda73e1-daf6-44ad-824f-ece0d70745bb","ref":{"parent":"a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-12-12","docId":"75","text":"11.04.010 Purpose.","id":"2cda73e1-daf6-44ad-824f-ece0d70745bb","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/2cda73e1-daf6-44ad-824f-ece0d70745bb\/8c4cfd2e-6f89-49ef-a8e5-64bfd0109f50","ref":{"parent":"2cda73e1-daf6-44ad-824f-ece0d70745bb","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-12-12-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EIn addition to and in accordance with the determination made and the authority granted under Vehicle Code Section 22660 to abate and remove abandoned, wrecked, dismantled or inoperative vehicles or parts thereof as public nuisances, the City Council finds that the accumulation and storage of abandoned, wrecked, dismantled or inoperative vehicles or parts on private or public property, not including highways, creates a condition tending to reduce the value of private property, promote blight and deterioration, invite plundering, create fire hazards and harbors for rodents and insects, constitute attractive nuisances creating a hazard to the health and safety of minors and to be injurious to the public\u2019s health, safety and general welfare. Thus, the presence of an abandoned, wrecked, dismantled or inoperative vehicle or part on private or public property, except as expressly provided, is declared to constitute a public nuisance which may be abated and removed in accordance with the provisions of this chapter.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1672, \u00a7 2(A), 1995; Ord. 756, (part), 1976; Ord. 413, \u00a7 1, 1968)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"8c4cfd2e-6f89-49ef-a8e5-64bfd0109f50","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/67af70f6-0959-495c-96c9-288ca036467f","ref":{"parent":"a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-12-13","docId":"75","text":"11.04.011 Definitions.","id":"67af70f6-0959-495c-96c9-288ca036467f","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/67af70f6-0959-495c-96c9-288ca036467f\/29a6519e-34bc-4339-a219-d894302e2332","ref":{"parent":"67af70f6-0959-495c-96c9-288ca036467f","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-12-13-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Col class=\u0022default-style\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:upper-alpha\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u201cAbandoned vehicle\u201d includes:\u003Col\u003E\u003Cli\u003EAny vehicle or part that is parked, stored or left on public or private property in such inoperable or neglected condition that the owner\u2019s intention to relinquish all rights or interest in it may be reasonably concluded.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EAny vehicle or part that is wrecked, dismantled or inoperative and that is parked, stored or left on public or private property, except as provided in Section 11.04.020 of this chapter.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u201cCost of abatement\u201d means all costs incurred in the abatement and removal of a vehicle or part including, but not limited to, hearing costs, staff costs, legal costs, overhead, administration, appeal costs, assessment confirmation hearing costs, towing and removal costs, and costs of storage and sale.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u201cDesignated employee\u201d means employees of the City whose duties include enforcement of this chapter.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u201cDismantled vehicle\u201d means any vehicle that is partially or wholly disassembled.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u201cHighway\u201d means a road, street or other passage maintained and open to use by the public for purposes of vehicular travel.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u201cInoperative vehicle\u201d means any vehicle that cannot be moved under its own power.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u201cOfficer\u201d means a peace officer as defined in Chapter 4.5 (commencing with Section 830) of Title 3 of Part 2 of the Penal Code, or any employee of the Sheriff\u2019s Department or California Highway Patrol designated to enforce the provisions of this chapter.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u201cOwner of the land\u201d means the owner of the land on which the vehicle or part is located as shown on the last equalized assessment roll.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u201cOwner of the vehicle\u201d means the last registered owner and legal owner of record.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u201cPublic property\u201d does not include highways.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u201cVehicle\u201d means a device by which someone or something is carried or transported on a highway, except a device moved by human power or used exclusively on stationary rails or tracks. \u201cVehicle\u201d includes the component parts of such device and applies to registered and unregistered vehicles.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u201cWrecked vehicle\u201d means any vehicle that is damaged to such an extent that it cannot be operated safely upon the highway.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1676, \u00a7 2(B), 1995)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"29a6519e-34bc-4339-a219-d894302e2332","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/035d68ec-cbe7-49e2-b3ea-8d455b7ed2df","ref":{"parent":"a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-12-14","docId":"75","text":"11.04.019 Acts Prohibited.","id":"035d68ec-cbe7-49e2-b3ea-8d455b7ed2df","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/035d68ec-cbe7-49e2-b3ea-8d455b7ed2df\/dc071588-fe9f-4ec9-b3b6-ebe12ccc0159","ref":{"parent":"035d68ec-cbe7-49e2-b3ea-8d455b7ed2df","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-12-14-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003ENo person shall commit or cause to be committed any of the following acts:\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Col class=\u0022default-style\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:upper-alpha\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003EAbandon or permit the abandonment of a vehicle or part on private or public property.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EPark, store, leave or permit the parking, storage or leaving of a vehicle or part on private or public property in such inoperative or neglected condition that it can be reasonably concluded that all rights or interests of the owner in such vehicle or part have been relinquished.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EPark, store, leave or permit the parking, storing or leaving of any vehicle in a wrecked, dismantled or inoperative condition on private or public property.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1676, \u00a7 2(C), 1995)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"dc071588-fe9f-4ec9-b3b6-ebe12ccc0159","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/c44fad25-d398-400f-82c3-07ed360da541","ref":{"parent":"a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-12-15","docId":"75","text":"11.04.020 Exception to Acts Prohibited.","id":"c44fad25-d398-400f-82c3-07ed360da541","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/c44fad25-d398-400f-82c3-07ed360da541\/b75f3d31-e1c0-4c72-8535-9f75e818eb0f","ref":{"parent":"c44fad25-d398-400f-82c3-07ed360da541","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-12-15-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EThis chapter shall not apply to:\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Col class=\u0022default-style\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:upper-alpha\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003EA vehicle or part which is either completely enclosed within a building, or is situated within the backyard of any premises and screened in such a manner that it is not visible from the street or other public or private property.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EA vehicle or part which is stored or parked in a lawful manner on private property in connection with the business of a licensed dismantler, licensed vehicle dealer, a junk dealer, or when such storage or parking is necessary to the operation of a lawfully conducted business.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003ENothing in this section shall authorize the maintenance of a public or private nuisance.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1676, \u00a7 2(D), 1995; Ord. 758, 1976; Ord. 413, \u00a7 2, 1968)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"b75f3d31-e1c0-4c72-8535-9f75e818eb0f","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/060ecf2e-1457-4dbc-8f43-3d8afa3decc3","ref":{"parent":"a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-12-16","docId":"75","text":"11.04.030 Nonexclusiveness.","id":"060ecf2e-1457-4dbc-8f43-3d8afa3decc3","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/060ecf2e-1457-4dbc-8f43-3d8afa3decc3\/4299144e-5440-40ee-95e7-99cdc80cdf94","ref":{"parent":"060ecf2e-1457-4dbc-8f43-3d8afa3decc3","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-12-16-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EThis chapter is not the exclusive regulation of abandoned, wrecked, dismantled or inoperative vehicles within the City; other state, county and local regulatory codes, statutes, and ordinances also apply.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1676, \u00a7 2(E), 1995; Ord. 413, \u00a7 3, 1968)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"4299144e-5440-40ee-95e7-99cdc80cdf94","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/12f1a374-8765-4233-81dd-34d7a06f345e","ref":{"parent":"a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-12-17","docId":"75","text":"11.04.031 Violation Constitutes Public Nuisance Subject to Nuisance Abatement Procedure.","id":"12f1a374-8765-4233-81dd-34d7a06f345e","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/12f1a374-8765-4233-81dd-34d7a06f345e\/9f184376-7792-4b1c-8ae0-57340644e547","ref":{"parent":"12f1a374-8765-4233-81dd-34d7a06f345e","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-12-17-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EAny violation of this chapter is declared to be a public nuisance and subject to abatement and the imposition of a special assessment and lien to recover any costs of abatement in accordance with the procedures prescribed in this chapter.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1676, \u00a7 2(F), 1995)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"9f184376-7792-4b1c-8ae0-57340644e547","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/04ebca91-c8d5-450b-aacf-c71c7f74afc5","ref":{"parent":"a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-12-18","docId":"75","text":"11.04.040 Enforcement, Administration by City Manager\u2013Authority to Enter Private Property\u2013Authority to Remove Abandoned Vehicles.","id":"04ebca91-c8d5-450b-aacf-c71c7f74afc5","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/04ebca91-c8d5-450b-aacf-c71c7f74afc5\/9ff96622-0f8f-460c-a54e-753dbf48d63f","ref":{"parent":"04ebca91-c8d5-450b-aacf-c71c7f74afc5","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-12-18-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Col class=\u0022default-style\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:upper-alpha\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe City Manager, his designated employees and any officer are responsible for enforcing the provisions of this chapter. Designated employees, pursuant to Penal Code Section 830.12, and any officer shall have the power to issue citations for any violation of this chapter and of Vehicle Code Section 22523. No person shall exercise the power to issue citations without first meeting the minimum training requirements of Penal Code Section 832(a). The City Manager shall administer the provisions of this chapter.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EIn the enforcement of this chapter, a designated employee or officer may enter private property, subject to warrant requirements under law, to examine a vehicle or part, to obtain information on the identity of a vehicle, or to remove or cause the removal of a vehicle or part pursuant to the provisions of this chapter.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EPursuant to authority under Government Code Section 22660, if a designated employee or officer has reasonable grounds to believe that a vehicle or part has been abandoned, or that a wrecked, dismantled or inoperative vehicle or part has been parked, stored or left on public or private property in violation of the provisions of this chapter, the designated employee or officer may abate and remove the vehicle or part as a public nuisance in accordance with the procedures prescribed in this chapter.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EPursuant to authority under Vehicle Code Section 22669, if a designated employee or officer has reasonable grounds to believe that a vehicle has been abandoned, as determined under Vehicle Code Section 22523, the designated employee or officer, without the express consent of the owner or person in lawful possession or control of the property, may remove the vehicle from public or private property.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1676, \u00a7 2(G), 1995; Ord. 413, \u00a7 4, 1968)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"9ff96622-0f8f-460c-a54e-753dbf48d63f","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/ae857565-aeb2-49ba-baae-3512309a2eb1","ref":{"parent":"a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-12-19","docId":"75","text":"11.04.050 Authority of Contractor to Remove Abandoned Vehicles from Private or Public Property.","id":"ae857565-aeb2-49ba-baae-3512309a2eb1","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/ae857565-aeb2-49ba-baae-3512309a2eb1\/22c8711c-0cd0-4a8d-9171-191e8bcea521","ref":{"parent":"ae857565-aeb2-49ba-baae-3512309a2eb1","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-12-19-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EWhen the City Council has contracted with or granted a franchise to any person to carry out the purpose of this chapter, such person may remove a vehicle or part from private or public property, after determination by a designated employee or officer, that the vehicle or part is abandoned. Such person may enter upon private or public property, subject to warrant requirements under law, to remove or cause the removal of a vehicle or part pursuant to the provisions of this chapter.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1676, \u00a7 2(H), 1995; Ord. 413, \u00a7 5, 1968)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"22c8711c-0cd0-4a8d-9171-191e8bcea521","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/a91e9ea7-5d7d-4cfc-acb6-bd21102258e7","ref":{"parent":"a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-12-210","docId":"75","text":"11.04.060 Administrative Costs.","id":"a91e9ea7-5d7d-4cfc-acb6-bd21102258e7","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/a91e9ea7-5d7d-4cfc-acb6-bd21102258e7\/d058f41f-8f98-483f-857a-2601a09a4981","ref":{"parent":"a91e9ea7-5d7d-4cfc-acb6-bd21102258e7","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-12-210-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EThe City Council shall from time to time determine and fix an amount to be assessed as administrative costs (excluding the actual cost of removal of any vehicle or part thereof) under this chapter.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 413, \u00a7 6, 1968)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"d058f41f-8f98-483f-857a-2601a09a4981","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/2fb59b93-5629-487b-a2b2-5454e627b8ae","ref":{"parent":"a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-12-211","docId":"75","text":"11.04.062 Notice of Intention to Abate and Remove.","id":"2fb59b93-5629-487b-a2b2-5454e627b8ae","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/2fb59b93-5629-487b-a2b2-5454e627b8ae\/a5154b49-876e-496c-a0db-3920ae9d5b46","ref":{"parent":"2fb59b93-5629-487b-a2b2-5454e627b8ae","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-12-211-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Col class=\u0022default-style\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:upper-alpha\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe City shall give notice of intention to abate and remove a vehicle or part as a public nuisance not less than ten days before such abatement and removal. The notice of intention to abate and remove shall fulfill the requirements of this section and shall basically be in the following form:\u003Cbr\u003E\n\u003Cbr\u003E\nNOTICE OF INTENTION TO ABATE AND REMOVE\u003Cbr\u003E\n\u003Cbr\u003E\n[Name and address of Owner of the Land\/Owner of the Vehicle]\u003Cbr\u003E\n\u003Cbr\u003E\nAs owner of the above-referenced [property\/vehicle], you are hereby notified that the City of Cupertino has determined that an abandoned, wrecked, dismantled or inoperative vehicle or part, described as [vehicle make, model, license number] exists on the property located at . The maintenance of this vehicle or part constitutes a public nuisance in violation of Chapter 11.04 of the Cupertino Municipal Code.\u003Cbr\u003E\n\u003Cbr\u003E\nYou have 10 days from the date of this Notice to abate this nuisance by removing the vehicle or part described herein from the above-described property. If you do not abate this nuisance within the 10-day period, the City is authorized to do or cause to be done whatever work is necessary to abate the nuisance [and to assess the costs of abatement, together with administrative costs, against your property].\u003Cbr\u003E\n\u003Cbr\u003E\nYOU ARE FURTHER NOTIFIED that you may request a public hearing within 10 days from the date of this Notice. If a written request for a public hearing is not received by the City Clerk with the 10-day period, the City is authorized to abate the public nuisance [and assess the costs of abatement] without a hearing. [If a public hearing is requested, you may appear in person or you may submit a sworn written statement in lieu of attendance.] Where the City has abated or caused the abatement of the vehicle, the vehicle shall be stored at a disposal yard for 15 days, after which if the vehicle is not claimed, it may be destroyed or dismantled and sold as scrap pursuant to Chapter 11.04 of the Cupertino Municipal Code.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EException to Notice Requirement. A notice of intention to abate and remove is not required for removal of a vehicle or part which is inoperable due to the absence of a motor, transmission or wheels, incapable of being towed, and:\u003Col\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe vehicle or part is valued at less than two hundred dollars ($200) by a person specified in Vehicle Code Section 22855, or\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe vehicle or part is determined to be a public nuisance presenting an immediate threat to public health or safety, or\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe property owner and the owner of the vehicle have signed releases authorizing removal and waiving further interest in the vehicle or part, or\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe inoperable vehicle is located upon a parcel that is (a) zoned for agricultural use, or (b) not improved with a residential structure.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe notice of intention to abate and remove shall contain a statement of the following:\u003Col\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThat the vehicle or part has been declared a public nuisance;\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe hearing rights of the owner of the vehicle or part and of the owner of the property;\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003ENotice to the property owner that he\/she may appear in person at a hearing or may submit a sworn written statement denying responsibility for the presence of the vehicle or part on the land, including reasons for such denial, in lieu of appearing; and\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThat a vehicle abated by the City may be dismantled or destroyed pursuant to Section 11.04.140.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EService. The notice of intention to abate and remove shall be mailed, by registered or certified mail, to the owner of the land as shown on the last equalized assessment roll, and to the last registered and legal owners of record of the vehicle unless the vehicle or part is in such condition that identification numbers are not available to determine ownership. The notice of intention to abate and remove may also be served in person by a designated employee. When personal service is utilized, the owner of the land or vehicle shall acknowledge service by signature.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EPosting. If the vehicle or part to be abated is located on private property, the notice of intention to abate and remove shall be conspicuously posted on the property.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1676, \u00a7 2(J), 1995; Ord. 756, (part), 1976)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"a5154b49-876e-496c-a0db-3920ae9d5b46","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/5a067767-539e-4178-9143-f17cf584104d","ref":{"parent":"a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-12-212","docId":"75","text":"11.04.070 Public Hearing upon Request of Owner.","id":"5a067767-539e-4178-9143-f17cf584104d","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/5a067767-539e-4178-9143-f17cf584104d\/70520814-784a-454d-9367-46fa2704c949","ref":{"parent":"5a067767-539e-4178-9143-f17cf584104d","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-12-212-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Col class=\u0022default-style\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:upper-alpha\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003EWhen requested in writing by the owner of the vehicle or the owner of the land within ten days after the date of the notice of intention to abate and remove, a public hearing shall be held before the City Council on whether the vehicle or part is abandoned, wrecked, dismantled or inoperative and constitutes a public nuisance under this chapter.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EIf the owner of the land submits a sworn written statement denying responsibility for the presence of the vehicle or part on the land within the ten-day period, that statement shall be construed as a request for a public hearing which does not require the presence of the owner of the land.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EIf a request for a public hearing is not received within the ten-day period, the designated employee or officer shall have authority to remove the vehicle or part in the manner provided by this chapter, and collect the costs of abatement as prescribed in Section 1.09.090 of this code or in any other manner allowed by law.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1676, \u00a7 2(K), 1995; Ord. 756, (part), 1976)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"70520814-784a-454d-9367-46fa2704c949","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/1b07994f-0199-4507-af8a-ddd0aa48a88d","ref":{"parent":"a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-12-213","docId":"75","text":"11.04.090 Public Nuisance Abatement Hearing Procedure and Findings.","id":"1b07994f-0199-4507-af8a-ddd0aa48a88d","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/1b07994f-0199-4507-af8a-ddd0aa48a88d\/8e72a7ee-282b-4d98-855e-7dacadb84d09","ref":{"parent":"1b07994f-0199-4507-af8a-ddd0aa48a88d","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-12-213-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Col class=\u0022default-style\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:upper-alpha\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe hearing shall be conducted in accordance with the procedures set forth in Section 1.09.070B of this code.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe owner of the land may appear in person at the hearing or submit a sworn written statement denying responsibility for the presence of the vehicle on the land, with reasons for such denial.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EAt the conclusion of the hearing, the Council shall reverse, modify or affirm the determinations of the City Manager and make such orders and confirmation of costs as appropriate. The decision shall be in writing, contain findings of fact and be filed with the City Clerk within five working days from the conclusion of the hearing. Where a nuisance is declared, the decision shall contain a finding that the vehicle or part was \u201cabandoned, wrecked, dismantled or inoperative\u201d thereby constituting a public nuisance, include the basis for that finding and order the abatement and removal of the vehicle or part. A copy of the decision shall be sent to each party appearing at the hearing, and if no appearance was made by the appellant, to the address provided on the appeal. The decision of the Council shall be final when filed with the City Clerk.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EIf the Council determines that the vehicle or part was placed on the land without the consent of the owner of the land and that the landowner has not subsequently acquiesced in its presence, then the cost of abatement of the vehicle shall not be assessed against the land, nor shall any other attempt be made to collect such costs from the landowner.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1676, \u00a7 2(M), 1995; Ord. 1027, (part), 1980; Ord. 413, \u00a7 9, 1968)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"8e72a7ee-282b-4d98-855e-7dacadb84d09","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/5f5c6861-8701-4727-a8fc-083b6115cc5d","ref":{"parent":"a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-12-214","docId":"75","text":"11.04.091 Time for Compliance.","id":"5f5c6861-8701-4727-a8fc-083b6115cc5d","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/5f5c6861-8701-4727-a8fc-083b6115cc5d\/eb7207b9-de8e-4b7d-b1cb-2abd1f0be8cd","ref":{"parent":"5f5c6861-8701-4727-a8fc-083b6115cc5d","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-12-214-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EIf the Council finds a public nuisance, the owner of the vehicle or the owner of the land shall comply with the Council\u2019s order to abate and remove within such period of time as may be prescribed, and in the absence of any prescribed time, within thirty days from the date of final determination.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1676, \u00a7 2(N), 1995)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"eb7207b9-de8e-4b7d-b1cb-2abd1f0be8cd","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/dac90a35-492a-4d27-ae5a-11f9b591e25e","ref":{"parent":"a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-12-215","docId":"75","text":"11.04.092 Noncompliance with Order to Abate\u2013Abatement and Collection of Costs.","id":"dac90a35-492a-4d27-ae5a-11f9b591e25e","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/dac90a35-492a-4d27-ae5a-11f9b591e25e\/e6a105d2-2608-436a-b75b-320fc990be02","ref":{"parent":"dac90a35-492a-4d27-ae5a-11f9b591e25e","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-12-215-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EUpon the failure or refusal to comply with the order to abate within the prescribed time period, the designated employee or officer shall abate and remove the vehicle or part. An account of the cost of abatement shall be kept for each separate assessor\u2019s parcel involved in the abatement and shall be posted on the property in the manner prescribed in Section 1.09.090 of this code.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EWhere the City has accomplished the abatement, or has paid for the abatement work, the actual cost thereof, together with an administrative cost, including reasonable attorneys\u2019 fees, shall be charged to the owner of the property. The combined amounts shall be included in a bill and sent by mail to the owner for payment, if not previously paid. The bill shall apprise the owner that failure to pay the bill within fifteen days from the date of mailing may result in a lien upon the property.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EIf the bill is not paid within the fifteen-day period, the City shall collect the costs of abatement as prescribed in Sections 1.09.090 of this code or in any other manner allowed by law.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1676, \u00a7 2(O), 1995)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"e6a105d2-2608-436a-b75b-320fc990be02","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/47ef1121-e7d1-4c99-94ac-91fb492326e3","ref":{"parent":"a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-12-216","docId":"75","text":"11.04.100 Post removal notice to Department of Motor Vehicles.","id":"47ef1121-e7d1-4c99-94ac-91fb492326e3","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/47ef1121-e7d1-4c99-94ac-91fb492326e3\/8dc6c00c-d7d1-4111-8fd3-6b8db9502696","ref":{"parent":"47ef1121-e7d1-4c99-94ac-91fb492326e3","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-12-216-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EWritten notice shall be given to the Department of Motor Vehicles within five days after the date of removal. The notice shall identify the vehicle or part and any known evidence of registration.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1676, \u00a7 2(P), 1995; Ord. 413, \u00a7 10, 1968)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"8dc6c00c-d7d1-4111-8fd3-6b8db9502696","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/cafa5a3d-cf88-4389-9184-8797d11e33fc","ref":{"parent":"a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-12-217","docId":"75","text":"11.04.110 Notice to Owner of Vehicle Removed Pursuant to Section 11.04.062b Prior to Final Disposition.","id":"cafa5a3d-cf88-4389-9184-8797d11e33fc","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/cafa5a3d-cf88-4389-9184-8797d11e33fc\/968d955e-0ec9-43bd-9eb8-b1661f2fa6e5","ref":{"parent":"cafa5a3d-cf88-4389-9184-8797d11e33fc","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-12-217-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EPrior to final disposition under Section 11.04.120 of a vehicle or part removed without notice pursuant to Section 11.04.062B, notice of intent to dispose of the vehicle or part shall be mailed to the registered and legal owners of the vehicle or part. The notice shall include the location where the vehicle may be claimed, the date before which the claim must be made and the City\u2019s authority for removal of the vehicle. If the vehicle or part is not claimed and removed within fifteen calendar days after notice is mailed, from a location specified in Section 11.04.120, final disposition under Section 11.04.140 may proceed.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1676, \u00a7 2(Q), 1995; Ord. 1027, (part), 1980; Ord. 756, (part), 1976; Ord. 413, \u00a7 11, 1968)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"968d955e-0ec9-43bd-9eb8-b1661f2fa6e5","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/b0b01eef-3646-44f6-99b1-c74e060de626","ref":{"parent":"a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-12-218","docId":"75","text":"11.04.120 Disposition of Vehicle\u2013Removal to Disposal Yard.","id":"b0b01eef-3646-44f6-99b1-c74e060de626","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/b0b01eef-3646-44f6-99b1-c74e060de626\/25fad0a3-a2ad-4264-a6fa-6fba65221e2d","ref":{"parent":"b0b01eef-3646-44f6-99b1-c74e060de626","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-12-218-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EAny vehicle or part removed pursuant to this chapter may be disposed of by removal to a scrapyard, licensed automobile dismantler\u2019s yard, garage or other place of safety where the vehicle shall be stored consistent with Section 11.04.130.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1676, \u00a7 2(R), 1995; Ord. 1027, (part), 1980)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"25fad0a3-a2ad-4264-a6fa-6fba65221e2d","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/75a69e00-d897-4438-afea-f5a6b68644f2","ref":{"parent":"a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-12-219","docId":"75","text":"11.04.130 Reconstruction of Vehicle after Removal Prohibited\u2013Exception.","id":"75a69e00-d897-4438-afea-f5a6b68644f2","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/75a69e00-d897-4438-afea-f5a6b68644f2\/063c32da-d161-4506-8a21-3a500db47721","ref":{"parent":"75a69e00-d897-4438-afea-f5a6b68644f2","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-12-219-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EAfter a vehicle has been removed it shall not be reconstructed or made operable, except a vehicle which qualifies for either horseless carriage license plates or historical vehicle license plates pursuant to Vehicle Code Section 5004, in which case the vehicle may be reconstructed or made operable.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1676, \u00a7 2(S), 1995; Ord. 1027, (part), 1980)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"063c32da-d161-4506-8a21-3a500db47721","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/d23e4c57-030a-447d-adc2-d97add064128","ref":{"parent":"a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-12-220","docId":"75","text":"11.04.140 Final Disposition of Vehicle after Storage.","id":"d23e4c57-030a-447d-adc2-d97add064128","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/d23e4c57-030a-447d-adc2-d97add064128\/24505a61-e334-4603-99e9-d37691c17ded","ref":{"parent":"d23e4c57-030a-447d-adc2-d97add064128","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-12-220-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EWhenever a vehicle has been removed to a disposal yard under Section 11.04.120, the vehicle shall be stored for a minimum of fifteen days. If the vehicle is not claimed by the owner within the fifteen days, the vehicle may be destroyed or dismantled and the parts may be sold as scrap. Any proceeds realized by the City from disposal of the vehicle shall be used to defray costs incurred under this chapter.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1676, \u00a7 2(T), 1995; Ord. 1027, (part), 1980)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"24505a61-e334-4603-99e9-d37691c17ded","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/318d9cb2-b29c-4166-8964-bda2485fb592","ref":{"parent":"a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-12-221","docId":"75","text":"11.04.150 Treble Costs of Abatement upon Repeated Violations.","id":"318d9cb2-b29c-4166-8964-bda2485fb592","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/318d9cb2-b29c-4166-8964-bda2485fb592\/670b8cd4-f260-4591-bb22-2641a0912a60","ref":{"parent":"318d9cb2-b29c-4166-8964-bda2485fb592","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-12-221-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EUpon entry of a second or subsequent civil or criminal judgment against a property owner within a two-year period for violations of this chapter, a court may order the owner to pay treble the costs of the abatement.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1676, \u00a7 2(U), 1995; Ord. 1027, (part), 1980; Ord. 590, \u00a7 1 (part), 1973; Ord. 413, \u00a7 12, 1968)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"670b8cd4-f260-4591-bb22-2641a0912a60","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/2b3e9093-d7db-40d4-b55d-8371fa21a6ce","ref":{"parent":"a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-12-222","docId":"75","text":"11.04.170 Violation\u2013Penalty.","id":"2b3e9093-d7db-40d4-b55d-8371fa21a6ce","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a40be004-db33-4cfe-8153-a7db95c97d35\/2b3e9093-d7db-40d4-b55d-8371fa21a6ce\/3536c8b4-4fda-40d5-8e5e-654d5db53ec2","ref":{"parent":"2b3e9093-d7db-40d4-b55d-8371fa21a6ce","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-12-222-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EIt is unlawful and an infraction for any person to fail or refuse to remove an abandoned, wrecked, dismantled or inoperative vehicle or part thereof or refuse to abate such nuisance when ordered to do so in accordance with the abatement provisions of this chapter or state law where such state law is applicable, and upon conviction of such infraction, shall be punished as provided in Chapter 1.12.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1027, (part), 1980; Ord. 413, \u00a7 14, 1968)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"3536c8b4-4fda-40d5-8e5e-654d5db53ec2","prev_id":null}]}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192","ref":{"parent":"ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":1,"tag":"h3"},"pos":"212-13","docId":"75","text":"CHAPTER 11.08: BICYCLES*","id":"7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/ad8736e0-b28a-4e61-90e8-3105fc5756a2","ref":{"parent":"7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-13-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003E* Prior ordinance history: Ords. 708, 741, 1068, 1071, 1173, 1228 and 1381.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E* For statutory provisions authorizing local authorities to pass ordinances not in conflict with state law with respect to the operation, use, licensing, and equipment of bicycles, see Veh. Code \u00a7 21206; for statutory provisions authorizing local authorities to establish bicycle lanes, and to regulate the operation of bicycles and vehicles with respect thereto, see Veh. Code \u00a7 21207; for statutory provisions setting forth certain equipment requirements for bicycles, see Veh Code \u00a7 21201 and Veh. Code \u00a7 21201.5; for statutory provisions relating to the registration and licensing of bicycles, see Veh. Code \u00a7 39000 et. seq.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"ad8736e0-b28a-4e61-90e8-3105fc5756a2","prev_id":null},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/835b932f-e568-45cf-83fb-7c17976b88e0","ref":{"parent":"7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-13-12","docId":"75","text":"11.08.010 Bicycle\u2013Definitions.","id":"835b932f-e568-45cf-83fb-7c17976b88e0","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/835b932f-e568-45cf-83fb-7c17976b88e0\/abdf626c-02db-412b-b889-7ba51da689fc","ref":{"parent":"835b932f-e568-45cf-83fb-7c17976b88e0","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-13-12-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003E\u201cBicycle,\u201d for the purposes of this chapter, means a device upon which any person may ride, propelled exclusively by human power through a belt, chain or gears having one or more wheels.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1420, (part), 1987)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"abdf626c-02db-412b-b889-7ba51da689fc","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/1673aed9-20c2-4f10-8da7-6ed5bbafffdb","ref":{"parent":"7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-13-13","docId":"75","text":"11.08.011 Motor-Driven Cycle.","id":"1673aed9-20c2-4f10-8da7-6ed5bbafffdb","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/1673aed9-20c2-4f10-8da7-6ed5bbafffdb\/462bff9e-ab84-4f1f-be83-6951f4bd63d6","ref":{"parent":"1673aed9-20c2-4f10-8da7-6ed5bbafffdb","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-13-13-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EA \u201cmotor-driven cycle\u201d is any motorcycle, including every motor scooter, with a motor which produces less than fifteen gross brake horsepower, and every bicycle with motor attached. \u201cMotor-driven cycle\u201d does not include a \u0022motorized bicycle\u0022 as defined in Section 11.08.012.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1420, (part), 1987)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"462bff9e-ab84-4f1f-be83-6951f4bd63d6","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/a5580b1c-8dbb-449c-955e-bbb89096587b","ref":{"parent":"7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-13-14","docId":"75","text":"11.08.012 Motorized Bicycle.","id":"a5580b1c-8dbb-449c-955e-bbb89096587b","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/a5580b1c-8dbb-449c-955e-bbb89096587b\/0ff2ce29-8cdc-4cbc-a85b-f3b3d2d7b409","ref":{"parent":"a5580b1c-8dbb-449c-955e-bbb89096587b","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-13-14-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EA \u201cmotorized bicycle\u201d or \u201cmoped\u201d is any two-wheeled or three-wheeled device having fully operational pedals for propulsion by human power, or having no pedals if powered solely by electrical energy, and an automatic transmission and a motor which produces less than two gross brake horsepower and is capable of propelling the device at a maximum speed of not more than thirty miles per hour on level ground.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1420, (part), 1987)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"0ff2ce29-8cdc-4cbc-a85b-f3b3d2d7b409","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/a2275107-50be-4a79-be27-d26a37325867","ref":{"parent":"7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-13-15","docId":"75","text":"11.08.013 Motorized Quadricycle.","id":"a2275107-50be-4a79-be27-d26a37325867","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/a2275107-50be-4a79-be27-d26a37325867\/9af7de84-795c-4791-ae47-52b77827e22c","ref":{"parent":"a2275107-50be-4a79-be27-d26a37325867","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-13-15-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EA \u201cmotorized quadricycle\u201d is a four-wheeled device designed to carry not more than two persons, including the driver, and having either an electric motor or a motor with an automatic transmission developing less than two gross brake horsepower and capable of propelling the device at a maximum speed of not more than thirty miles per hour on level ground. The device shall be utilized only by a person who by reason of physical disability is otherwise unable to move about as a pedestrian, or by a senior citizen as defined in Section 13000 of the California Vehicle Code.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1420, (part), 1987)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"9af7de84-795c-4791-ae47-52b77827e22c","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/5601b168-5eaf-4a33-8ee9-2a6205f1bcc8","ref":{"parent":"7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-13-16","docId":"75","text":"11.08.014 Roller Skates.","id":"5601b168-5eaf-4a33-8ee9-2a6205f1bcc8","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/5601b168-5eaf-4a33-8ee9-2a6205f1bcc8\/1df2d846-32b4-42ba-b47e-0cd9e47295cf","ref":{"parent":"5601b168-5eaf-4a33-8ee9-2a6205f1bcc8","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-13-16-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003E\u201cRoller skates\u201d are any footwear, or device which may be attached to the foot or footwear, to which wheels are attached, including wheels that are \u201cin line\u201d and where such wheels may be used to aid the wearer in moving or propulsion.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1767, (part), 1997)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"1df2d846-32b4-42ba-b47e-0cd9e47295cf","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/dde05a65-f3d6-4031-a0ba-118013eb6324","ref":{"parent":"7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-13-17","docId":"75","text":"11.08.015 Skateboard.","id":"dde05a65-f3d6-4031-a0ba-118013eb6324","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/dde05a65-f3d6-4031-a0ba-118013eb6324\/5c7a5d44-eb58-477c-a32d-8139896ecf76","ref":{"parent":"dde05a65-f3d6-4031-a0ba-118013eb6324","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-13-17-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003E\u201cSkateboard\u201d is any board of any material, which has wheels attached to it and is propelled or moved by human, gravitational, or mechanical power, and to which there is not fixed any device or mechanism to turn or control the wheels.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1767, (part), 1997)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"5c7a5d44-eb58-477c-a32d-8139896ecf76","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/e8778393-86be-43c3-bca5-87c90a49f7c7","ref":{"parent":"7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-13-18","docId":"75","text":"11.08.020 Reserved.","id":"e8778393-86be-43c3-bca5-87c90a49f7c7","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/e8778393-86be-43c3-bca5-87c90a49f7c7\/535f291d-211a-44a3-88f0-1f8a76196430","ref":{"parent":"e8778393-86be-43c3-bca5-87c90a49f7c7","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-13-18-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"535f291d-211a-44a3-88f0-1f8a76196430","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/041ca6b9-e4cd-4ad3-93e6-c0722fd7be11","ref":{"parent":"7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-13-19","docId":"75","text":"11.08.030 Administrative Authority.","id":"041ca6b9-e4cd-4ad3-93e6-c0722fd7be11","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/041ca6b9-e4cd-4ad3-93e6-c0722fd7be11\/215ad6ab-c053-43ac-89db-fd048981ed76","ref":{"parent":"041ca6b9-e4cd-4ad3-93e6-c0722fd7be11","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-13-19-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EThere are conferred upon the City Manager those powers and duties necessary for the administration of this chapter. In addition, there is also conferred upon the City Manager the authority and power to designate such officers and employees of the City, and of other cooperating public agencies, such as either the Central Fire District or the Sheriff\u2019s Department, as well as private persons such as bicycle retailers, as may be required to assist him in carrying out the intent and purpose of this chapter.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1420, (part), 1987)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"215ad6ab-c053-43ac-89db-fd048981ed76","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/92f01a90-84ae-4dc6-9d79-b19f2097cf09","ref":{"parent":"7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-13-210","docId":"75","text":"11.08.040 Reserved.","id":"92f01a90-84ae-4dc6-9d79-b19f2097cf09","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/92f01a90-84ae-4dc6-9d79-b19f2097cf09\/208ed061-e372-485a-9d5a-1679ee0b6cbe","ref":{"parent":"92f01a90-84ae-4dc6-9d79-b19f2097cf09","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-13-210-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"208ed061-e372-485a-9d5a-1679ee0b6cbe","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/78d5a26b-f42b-41e8-aea5-a902665b6110","ref":{"parent":"7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-13-211","docId":"75","text":"11.08.050 Reserved.","id":"78d5a26b-f42b-41e8-aea5-a902665b6110","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/78d5a26b-f42b-41e8-aea5-a902665b6110\/eef9de1f-dc02-4560-9fb8-50523039c101","ref":{"parent":"78d5a26b-f42b-41e8-aea5-a902665b6110","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-13-211-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"eef9de1f-dc02-4560-9fb8-50523039c101","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/4cb85956-3843-4271-81cf-aed84ccfa534","ref":{"parent":"7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-13-212","docId":"75","text":"11.08.060 Reserved.","id":"4cb85956-3843-4271-81cf-aed84ccfa534","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/4cb85956-3843-4271-81cf-aed84ccfa534\/95e1afde-1670-41c6-a98c-2ae58f405891","ref":{"parent":"4cb85956-3843-4271-81cf-aed84ccfa534","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-13-212-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"95e1afde-1670-41c6-a98c-2ae58f405891","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/e2ea05d6-7ae7-4f0c-b6c7-784da3040571","ref":{"parent":"7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-13-213","docId":"75","text":"11.08.061 Bicycle Serial Numbers and Identifying Marks \u2013 Prohibited Acts.","id":"e2ea05d6-7ae7-4f0c-b6c7-784da3040571","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/e2ea05d6-7ae7-4f0c-b6c7-784da3040571\/40da511a-1858-484a-961e-fe689f7deac9","ref":{"parent":"e2ea05d6-7ae7-4f0c-b6c7-784da3040571","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-13-213-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EIt is unlawful for any person to tamper with, destroy, mutilate or alter any serial number or the manufacturer\u2019s identifying marks on any bicycle frame.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 20-2214, 2020; Ord. 1420, (part), 1987)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"40da511a-1858-484a-961e-fe689f7deac9","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/cd39a3ed-7487-4e5b-874c-8cf2ee5334c7","ref":{"parent":"7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-13-214","docId":"75","text":"11.08.070 Reserved.","id":"cd39a3ed-7487-4e5b-874c-8cf2ee5334c7","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/cd39a3ed-7487-4e5b-874c-8cf2ee5334c7\/1aa4c061-a162-49de-be44-1c634d20c828","ref":{"parent":"cd39a3ed-7487-4e5b-874c-8cf2ee5334c7","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-13-214-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"1aa4c061-a162-49de-be44-1c634d20c828","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/bc71fcff-e1b2-4fc4-b597-3e0131081f07","ref":{"parent":"7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-13-215","docId":"75","text":"11.08.080 Reserved.","id":"bc71fcff-e1b2-4fc4-b597-3e0131081f07","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/bc71fcff-e1b2-4fc4-b597-3e0131081f07\/a1a703c3-cc7e-433f-9610-0de35b250521","ref":{"parent":"bc71fcff-e1b2-4fc4-b597-3e0131081f07","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-13-215-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"a1a703c3-cc7e-433f-9610-0de35b250521","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/e70250fe-531a-4b4b-b6a1-f5ee3c6aee13","ref":{"parent":"7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-13-216","docId":"75","text":"11.08.090 Reserved.","id":"e70250fe-531a-4b4b-b6a1-f5ee3c6aee13","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/e70250fe-531a-4b4b-b6a1-f5ee3c6aee13\/acffa22e-5e0a-4ee1-85f6-7d3c57ef5759","ref":{"parent":"e70250fe-531a-4b4b-b6a1-f5ee3c6aee13","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-13-216-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"acffa22e-5e0a-4ee1-85f6-7d3c57ef5759","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/d33b8dec-fd26-4146-ba0b-25ae8a3213e3","ref":{"parent":"7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-13-217","docId":"75","text":"11.08.100 Reserved.","id":"d33b8dec-fd26-4146-ba0b-25ae8a3213e3","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/d33b8dec-fd26-4146-ba0b-25ae8a3213e3\/7979f754-36c3-45df-b89a-4648c11e7d8a","ref":{"parent":"d33b8dec-fd26-4146-ba0b-25ae8a3213e3","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-13-217-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"7979f754-36c3-45df-b89a-4648c11e7d8a","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/3c3dfc8f-3921-4b65-8498-96fce3a273e3","ref":{"parent":"7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-13-218","docId":"75","text":"11.08.110 Reserved.","id":"3c3dfc8f-3921-4b65-8498-96fce3a273e3","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/3c3dfc8f-3921-4b65-8498-96fce3a273e3\/25d284d1-616a-4f87-8802-b3e3ce6db8fb","ref":{"parent":"3c3dfc8f-3921-4b65-8498-96fce3a273e3","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-13-218-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"25d284d1-616a-4f87-8802-b3e3ce6db8fb","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/19274272-b1e4-41ce-a3e7-ec567d6680e9","ref":{"parent":"7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-13-219","docId":"75","text":"11.08.120 Reserved.","id":"19274272-b1e4-41ce-a3e7-ec567d6680e9","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/19274272-b1e4-41ce-a3e7-ec567d6680e9\/ca172d9b-a40d-4086-a108-5c43e1391810","ref":{"parent":"19274272-b1e4-41ce-a3e7-ec567d6680e9","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-13-219-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"ca172d9b-a40d-4086-a108-5c43e1391810","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/3974cee1-4c52-40b7-ac19-5ba9d6a0b27d","ref":{"parent":"7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-13-220","docId":"75","text":"11.08.130 Equipment.","id":"3974cee1-4c52-40b7-ac19-5ba9d6a0b27d","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/3974cee1-4c52-40b7-ac19-5ba9d6a0b27d\/cbfff9db-302e-4fbb-bd06-b5716dfbe768","ref":{"parent":"3974cee1-4c52-40b7-ac19-5ba9d6a0b27d","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-13-220-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003ENo person shall operate a bicycle on any roadway or other property within the jurisdiction of the City unless it is equipped in conformance with Section 21201 of the California Vehicle Code.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1420, (part), 1987)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"cbfff9db-302e-4fbb-bd06-b5716dfbe768","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/3011f846-cdf6-4565-b47c-6340a049a880","ref":{"parent":"7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-13-221","docId":"75","text":"11.08.140 Laws Applicable to Bicycle Use.","id":"3011f846-cdf6-4565-b47c-6340a049a880","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/3011f846-cdf6-4565-b47c-6340a049a880\/89b525f5-a1ba-4b06-95c5-dd679902f1a3","ref":{"parent":"3011f846-cdf6-4565-b47c-6340a049a880","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-13-221-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EEvery person riding a bicycle upon a highway has all the rights and is subject to all the provisions applicable to the driver of a vehicle by this title, including, but not limited to, provisions dealing with driving under the influence of alcoholic beverages or drugs, and by the California Vehicle Code\u2019s Division 10 (commencing with Section 20000), Section 27400, Division 16.7 (commencing with Section 39000), Division 17 (commencing with Section 40000), except those provisions which by their very nature can have no application.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1420, (part), 1987)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"89b525f5-a1ba-4b06-95c5-dd679902f1a3","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/6a369b27-41a6-4b3e-96b8-18689502df81","ref":{"parent":"7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-13-222","docId":"75","text":"11.08.150 Operation on Roadway.","id":"6a369b27-41a6-4b3e-96b8-18689502df81","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/6a369b27-41a6-4b3e-96b8-18689502df81\/c036abe8-a4b7-481a-9832-20ca0767892f","ref":{"parent":"6a369b27-41a6-4b3e-96b8-18689502df81","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-13-222-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Col class=\u0022default-style\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:upper-alpha\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003EAny person operating a bicycle upon a roadway at a speed less than the normal speed of traffic moving in the same direction at such time shall ride as close as practicable to the right-hand curb or edge of the roadway, except under any of the following situations:\u003Col\u003E\u003Cli\u003EWhen overtaking and passing another bicycle or vehicle proceeding in the same direction;\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EWhen preparing for a left turn at an intersection or into a private road or driveway;\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EWhen reasonably necessary to avoid conditions (including, but not limited to, fixed or moving objects, vehicles, bicycles, pedestrians, animals, surface hazards or substandard width lanes) that make it unsafe to continue along the right-hand curb or edge, subject to the provisions of Section 21656. For purposes of this section, a \u201csubstandard width lane\u201d is a lane that is too narrow for a bicycle and a vehicle to travel safely side by side within the lane.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EAny person operating a bicycle upon a roadway of a highway, which highway carries traffic in one direction only and has two or more marked traffic lanes, may ride as near the left-hand curb or edge of such roadway as practicable.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1420, (part), 1987)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"c036abe8-a4b7-481a-9832-20ca0767892f","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/822ce31e-5fe7-4f6f-8745-60ab3c96b3b1","ref":{"parent":"7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-13-223","docId":"75","text":"11.08.160 Riding\u2013On Pedestrian Facilities.","id":"822ce31e-5fe7-4f6f-8745-60ab3c96b3b1","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/822ce31e-5fe7-4f6f-8745-60ab3c96b3b1\/d90ff7e6-7d32-48c0-999d-de321670fddf","ref":{"parent":"822ce31e-5fe7-4f6f-8745-60ab3c96b3b1","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-13-223-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003ENo person shall ride, use or operate a bicycle on any sidewalk within the City except as specifically permitted in this chapter.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 17-2161, 2017; Ord. 1649, 1994; Ord. 1560, 1991; Ord. 1420, (part), 1987)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"d90ff7e6-7d32-48c0-999d-de321670fddf","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/f8792031-c9aa-40d4-b974-a2a36c5da51d","ref":{"parent":"7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-13-224","docId":"75","text":"11.08.170 Hitching Rides.","id":"f8792031-c9aa-40d4-b974-a2a36c5da51d","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/f8792031-c9aa-40d4-b974-a2a36c5da51d\/68a31e7f-4f62-431b-bad1-6f6f513c6f3e","ref":{"parent":"f8792031-c9aa-40d4-b974-a2a36c5da51d","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-13-224-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003ENo person riding upon any motorcycle, motorized bicycle, bicycle, coaster, roller skates, sled or toy vehicle shall attach the same or herself\/himself to any streetcar or vehicle on the roadway.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1420, (part), 1987)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"68a31e7f-4f62-431b-bad1-6f6f513c6f3e","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/6674a7c9-39b8-4d6a-a822-196a06f51330","ref":{"parent":"7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-13-225","docId":"75","text":"11.08.180 Exemptions.","id":"6674a7c9-39b8-4d6a-a822-196a06f51330","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/6674a7c9-39b8-4d6a-a822-196a06f51330\/d982be4b-fd06-431e-873e-d14aaddfcfe6","ref":{"parent":"6674a7c9-39b8-4d6a-a822-196a06f51330","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-13-225-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EThe prohibition in Section 11.08.160 against riding, using, or operating a bicycle on a sidewalk shall not apply to the following:\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Col class=\u0022default-style\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:upper-alpha\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003EA child age twelve years and under.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EAn adult accompanying a child age twelve years and under who is also riding, using, or operating a bicycle.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EAny person riding, using or operating a bicycle on a pedestrian path, unless specifically posted as prohibited.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EAny person riding, using or operating a bicycle on the north side of Pacifica Drive, between Regnart Creek Trail and Torre Avenue.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EAny person riding, using or operating a bicycle on the east side of Finch Avenue, between Tilson Ave and 200 feet north of Calle de Barcelona.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 17-2161, 2017; Ord. 1420, (part), 1987; Ord. 24-2267, Att. A (part), 2024)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"d982be4b-fd06-431e-873e-d14aaddfcfe6","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/6a18ec15-5770-4201-9f15-08d42b04925e","ref":{"parent":"7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-13-226","docId":"75","text":"11.08.190 Permitted Movements from Bicycle Lanes.","id":"6a18ec15-5770-4201-9f15-08d42b04925e","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/6a18ec15-5770-4201-9f15-08d42b04925e\/3c450f21-9436-460a-900e-75251c4b46b7","ref":{"parent":"6a18ec15-5770-4201-9f15-08d42b04925e","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-13-226-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Col class=\u0022default-style\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:upper-alpha\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003EWhenever a bicycle lane has been established on a roadway pursuant to Section 21207 of the California Vehicle Code, any person operating a bicycle upon the roadway at a speed less than the normal speed of traffic moving in the same direction shall ride within the bicycle lane, except that such person may move out of the lane in any of the following situations:\u003Col\u003E\u003Cli\u003EWhen overtaking and passing another bicycle, vehicle or pedestrian within the lane or about to enter the lane if such overtaking and passing cannot be done safely within the lane;\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EWhen preparing for a left turn at an intersection or into a private road or driveway;\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EWhen reasonably necessary to leave the bicycle lane to avoid debris or other hazardous conditions.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003ENo person operating a bicycle shall leave a bicycle lane until the movement can be made with reasonable safety, and then only after giving an appropriate signal in the manner provided in Chapter 6 (commencing with Section 22100) of the California Vehicle Code in the event that any vehicle may be affected by the movement.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1420, (part), 1987)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"3c450f21-9436-460a-900e-75251c4b46b7","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/25e5b090-3368-4a13-a94b-576f20c9d67d","ref":{"parent":"7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-13-227","docId":"75","text":"11.08.200 Walking Bicycles.","id":"25e5b090-3368-4a13-a94b-576f20c9d67d","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/25e5b090-3368-4a13-a94b-576f20c9d67d\/6308a99f-5d81-4068-a1ec-c41738ffd34e","ref":{"parent":"25e5b090-3368-4a13-a94b-576f20c9d67d","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-13-227-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EBicycles may be walked at any time, subject to all provisions of law applicable to pedestrians.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1420, (part), 1987)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"6308a99f-5d81-4068-a1ec-c41738ffd34e","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/9fa9c141-624f-43a4-9573-a4414f0d9912","ref":{"parent":"7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-13-228","docId":"75","text":"11.08.210 Riding on Bicycles.","id":"9fa9c141-624f-43a4-9573-a4414f0d9912","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/9fa9c141-624f-43a4-9573-a4414f0d9912\/8bb90c39-a3a2-4d70-bd81-c63460c40e01","ref":{"parent":"9fa9c141-624f-43a4-9573-a4414f0d9912","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-13-228-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Col class=\u0022default-style\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:upper-alpha\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003ENo person operating a bicycle upon a highway shall ride other than upon or astride a permanent and regular seat attached thereto.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003ENo operator shall allow a person to ride as a passenger, and no person shall ride as a passenger, on a bicycle upon a highway other than upon or astride a separate seat attached thereto.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003Cp\u003EIf the passenger is a minor weighing forty pounds or less, the seat shall have adequate provision for retaining the minor in place and for protecting the minor from the moving parts of the bicycle.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1420, (part), 1987)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"8bb90c39-a3a2-4d70-bd81-c63460c40e01","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/14820f44-da64-48af-94f4-02bedb17e8d5","ref":{"parent":"7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-13-229","docId":"75","text":"11.08.220 Carrying Articles.","id":"14820f44-da64-48af-94f4-02bedb17e8d5","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/14820f44-da64-48af-94f4-02bedb17e8d5\/c7012a1e-a73f-49a9-9852-858fbf1b4f92","ref":{"parent":"14820f44-da64-48af-94f4-02bedb17e8d5","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-13-229-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003ENo person operating a bicycle shall carry any package, bundle or article which prevents the operator from keeping at least one hand upon the handlebars.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1420, (part), 1987)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"c7012a1e-a73f-49a9-9852-858fbf1b4f92","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/4e9074b5-f41a-49e8-b91d-f2011c7ecae0","ref":{"parent":"7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-13-230","docId":"75","text":"11.08.230 Motor Vehicles and Motorized Bicycles in Bicycle Lanes.","id":"4e9074b5-f41a-49e8-b91d-f2011c7ecae0","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/4e9074b5-f41a-49e8-b91d-f2011c7ecae0\/26540628-c355-47a1-8db7-197c1ed8f206","ref":{"parent":"4e9074b5-f41a-49e8-b91d-f2011c7ecae0","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-13-230-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Col class=\u0022default-style\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:upper-alpha\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003EWhenever a bicycle lane has been established on a roadway pursuant to Section 21207 of the California Vehicle Code, any person operating a motor vehicle on such roadway shall not drive in the bicycle lane except to park where parking is permitted, to enter or leave the highway, or to prepare for a turn.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThis section does not prohibit the use of a motorized bicycle in a bicycle lane pursuant to Section 21207.5 of the California Vehicle Code; provided, that no person shall operate a motorized bicycle upon a bicycle lane at a speed greater than is reasonable or prudent having due regard for visibility and the traffic on, and the surface of, the bicycle lane, and in no event in a manner which endangers the safety of bicyclists utilizing the bicycle lane.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1420, (part), 1987)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"26540628-c355-47a1-8db7-197c1ed8f206","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/79366455-b306-48de-b581-a6d05fa668e8","ref":{"parent":"7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-13-231","docId":"75","text":"11.08.240 Impoundment.","id":"79366455-b306-48de-b581-a6d05fa668e8","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/79366455-b306-48de-b581-a6d05fa668e8\/c737a489-6d0d-4037-8061-6f6f26b8a844","ref":{"parent":"79366455-b306-48de-b581-a6d05fa668e8","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-13-231-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EThe City may impound and retain possession of any bicycle in violation of the provisions of this chapter, and may retain possession of such bicycle until the provisions of this chapter are complied with. In addition, a fine may be imposed for any violation of this chapter pursuant to Section 11.08.310.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1420, (part), 1987)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"c737a489-6d0d-4037-8061-6f6f26b8a844","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/5d74de8b-12bb-43bd-ba53-d85ae6adbea7","ref":{"parent":"7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-13-232","docId":"75","text":"11.08.250 Bicycle Lanes\u2013Designated.","id":"5d74de8b-12bb-43bd-ba53-d85ae6adbea7","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/5d74de8b-12bb-43bd-ba53-d85ae6adbea7\/305d3d61-437d-4b95-99df-4b34f877298f","ref":{"parent":"5d74de8b-12bb-43bd-ba53-d85ae6adbea7","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-13-232-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EThe City Manager, upon approval of the City Council, is authorized to erect or place signs upon any street in the city indicating the existence of a bicycle lane, and otherwise regulating the location and use of vehicles and bicycles with respect to them, so long as the same are consistent with this chapter. Before such a sign is erected, the subject bicycle lane shall be designated on such streets by an approved painting or sign, or in such other manner as the City Manager shall determine will provide sufficient notice of the existence of such bicycle lane. When such a painting or sign is in place, no person shall disobey it.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EDESIGNATION OF BICYCLE LANES\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EStreet Description Side\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EFoothill Boulevard Freeway 280 to Stevens Creek\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBoulevard Both\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBubb Road Stevens Creek Boulevard to\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003ERainbow Drive Both\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EMary Avenue Meteor to Stevens Creek Boulevard Both\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EStelling Road Homestead Road to Rainbow Drive Both\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EKim Street Kirwin Lane to Bollinger Road Both\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBlaney Avenue Homestead to Stevens Creek\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBoulevard Both\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003ETantau Ave Homestead Road to Stevens\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003ECreek Boulevard Both\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EHomestead Road Grant Road to Swallow Drive Both\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EPruneridge Avenue Wolfe Road to Tantau Avenue Both\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EMariani Avenue De Anza Boulevard to Merritt Drive Both\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EVallco Parkway Wolfe Road to Tantau Avenue Both\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EMcClellan Road Byrne Avenue to Stelling Road Both\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBollinger Road Miller Avenue to Narciso Court Both\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003ERainbow Drive\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Saratoga-Sunnyvale\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003ERoad) Stelling Road to DeAnza Boulevard Both\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EStevens Creek\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBoulevard East City Limit to the West City Limit Both\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EDe Anza Boulevard Homestead Road to State Route 85 Both\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003ESouth Stelling Road Homestead Road to Prospect Road Both\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EProspect Road Stelling Road to De Anza Boulevard Both\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EMiller Avenue Calle De Barcelona To Bollinger Road Both\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EWolfe Road Homestead Road to Stevens Creek Boulevard Both\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EFoothill Boulevard Interstate Route 280 to McClellan Road Both\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBollinger Road Westlynn Way to the East City Limit Both\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBlaney Avenue Stevens Creek Boulevard to Bollinger Road Both\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EDe Anza Boulevard Homestead Road to Bollinger Road Both\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EDe Anza Boulevard State Route 85 to Prospect Road Both\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003ERodrigues Avenue De Anza Boulevard to Blaney Avenue Both\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003ETorre Avenue Stevens Creek Boulevard to Rodrigues Avenue Both\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 14-2120; Ord. 2091, 2012; Ord. 2063, 2010; Ord. 1873, 2001; Ord. 1870, 2001; Ord. 1856, 2000; Ord. 1848, 2000; Ord. 1766, 1997; Ord. 1759, 1997; Ord. 1745, 1996; Ord. 1740, 1996; Ord. 1731 (part), 1996; Ord. 1544, 1991; Ord. 1517, 1990; Ord. 1420 (part), 1987)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"305d3d61-437d-4b95-99df-4b34f877298f","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/46874ba2-dd97-47e7-bd5c-c0bee1ccbed2","ref":{"parent":"7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-13-233","docId":"75","text":"11.08.260 Bicycle Route\u2013Designated.","id":"46874ba2-dd97-47e7-bd5c-c0bee1ccbed2","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/46874ba2-dd97-47e7-bd5c-c0bee1ccbed2\/ac92b9f1-291e-46b7-b9d9-4127777f2dcc","ref":{"parent":"46874ba2-dd97-47e7-bd5c-c0bee1ccbed2","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-13-233-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EThe City Manager, upon approval of the City Council, is authorized to erect or place signs upon any street in the City indicating the existence of a bicycle route, and otherwise regulating the location and use of vehicles and bicycles with respect to them, so long as the same are consistent with this chapter. Before such a sign is erected, the subject bicycle route shall be designated on such streets by an approved sign, or in such other manner as the City Manager determines will provide sufficient notice of the existence of such bicycle route.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Ctable style=\u0022width:600px\u0022\u003E\u003Cthead\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Cth colspan=\u00223\u0022 scope=\u0022col\u0022\u003E\u003Cst