ion"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-13-234-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EIt is unlawful and subject to punishment in accordance with Section 11.08.280 of this chapter, for any person utilizing or riding upon any skateboard, roller skates or any similar device to ride or move about in or on any public property when the same property has been designated by the City Council and posted as a \u201cNo Skateboarding or Roller Skating Area.\u201d The following are established as a no skateboarding or roller skating areas:\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003ECivil Center Plaza (City Hall\/Library).\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EVeteran\u2019s Memorial (in Memorial Park).\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 2026, 2008; Ord. 1916, (part), 2003; Ord. 1898, 2002; Ord. 1767, (part), 1997)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"e0c930bc-852d-4bc6-a6be-a6c6e737006a","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/f4f8dc6d-2ff9-4e7e-889e-8e970d93f9ae","ref":{"parent":"7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-13-235","docId":"75","text":"11.08.280 Penalty.","id":"f4f8dc6d-2ff9-4e7e-889e-8e970d93f9ae","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7b698e2d-a313-4025-8455-2464c0a64192\/f4f8dc6d-2ff9-4e7e-889e-8e970d93f9ae\/073d7339-d99d-4d99-8477-ca1a9052e471","ref":{"parent":"f4f8dc6d-2ff9-4e7e-889e-8e970d93f9ae","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-13-235-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EAny person who violates any provision of this chapter shall be guilty of an infraction, and, upon conviction thereof, shall be punished as provided in Chapter 1.12, except that no fine imposed for violation of any licensing and registration provisions of this chapter shall exceed ten dollars.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1886, (part), 2001; Ord. 1767, (part), 1997; Ord. 1420, (part), 1987)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"073d7339-d99d-4d99-8477-ca1a9052e471","prev_id":null}]}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/ecb3b263-7de7-4f52-a7d4-ff7a28eb9ae7","ref":{"parent":"ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":1,"tag":"h3"},"pos":"212-14","docId":"75","text":"CHAPTER 11.09: PEDESTRIANS","id":"ecb3b263-7de7-4f52-a7d4-ff7a28eb9ae7","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/ecb3b263-7de7-4f52-a7d4-ff7a28eb9ae7\/f29c8de2-bcc2-45f5-8342-e2c9ed2093d9","ref":{"parent":"ecb3b263-7de7-4f52-a7d4-ff7a28eb9ae7","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-14-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"f29c8de2-bcc2-45f5-8342-e2c9ed2093d9","prev_id":null},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/ecb3b263-7de7-4f52-a7d4-ff7a28eb9ae7\/fe91d119-f2c9-478e-894e-b1c0b0131c81","ref":{"parent":"ecb3b263-7de7-4f52-a7d4-ff7a28eb9ae7","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-14-12","docId":"75","text":"11.09.010 Pedestrian\u2013Definitions.","id":"fe91d119-f2c9-478e-894e-b1c0b0131c81","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/ecb3b263-7de7-4f52-a7d4-ff7a28eb9ae7\/fe91d119-f2c9-478e-894e-b1c0b0131c81\/aac8ea18-ec82-48a5-9c66-ccadf8d3577c","ref":{"parent":"fe91d119-f2c9-478e-894e-b1c0b0131c81","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-14-12-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EA pedestrian in any person who is afoot or who is using a means of conveyance propelled by human power other than a bicycle.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1417, (part), 1987)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"aac8ea18-ec82-48a5-9c66-ccadf8d3577c","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/ecb3b263-7de7-4f52-a7d4-ff7a28eb9ae7\/5a0ea7d4-6ede-479a-ad4f-168690b3e3bf","ref":{"parent":"ecb3b263-7de7-4f52-a7d4-ff7a28eb9ae7","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-14-13","docId":"75","text":"11.09.020 Administrative authority.","id":"5a0ea7d4-6ede-479a-ad4f-168690b3e3bf","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/ecb3b263-7de7-4f52-a7d4-ff7a28eb9ae7\/5a0ea7d4-6ede-479a-ad4f-168690b3e3bf\/97aa5b87-8843-48ff-9e8b-99d968f23b80","ref":{"parent":"5a0ea7d4-6ede-479a-ad4f-168690b3e3bf","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-14-13-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EThere are conferred upon the City Manager those powers and duties necessary for the administration of this chapter. In addition, there is also conferred upon the City Manager the authority and power to designate such officers and employees of the City, and of other cooperating public agencies, such as the Sheriff\u2019s Department, as may be required to assist him in carrying out the intent and purpose of this chapter.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1417, (part), 1987)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"97aa5b87-8843-48ff-9e8b-99d968f23b80","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/ecb3b263-7de7-4f52-a7d4-ff7a28eb9ae7\/1d97129e-dff5-4623-9516-8ccbb9f6cb1e","ref":{"parent":"ecb3b263-7de7-4f52-a7d4-ff7a28eb9ae7","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-14-14","docId":"75","text":"11.09.050 Warrants for Adult Crossing Guards.","id":"1d97129e-dff5-4623-9516-8ccbb9f6cb1e","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/ecb3b263-7de7-4f52-a7d4-ff7a28eb9ae7\/1d97129e-dff5-4623-9516-8ccbb9f6cb1e\/56469d99-7a5d-4d12-9cff-518623d0bc23","ref":{"parent":"1d97129e-dff5-4623-9516-8ccbb9f6cb1e","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-14-14-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EAdult crossing guards normally are assigned where official supervision of elementary school pedestrians is desirable while they cross a public highway on a \u201csuggested route to school,\u201d and at least forty elementary school pedestrians for each of any two hours daily use the crossing while going to or from school. Adult crossing guards may be warranted under the following conditions:\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Col class=\u0022default-style\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:upper-alpha\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003EAt uncontrolled crossings where there is no alternate controlled crossing within six hundred feet, and:\u003Col\u003E\u003Cli\u003EIn urban areas where the vehicular traffic volume exceeds three hundred fifty in each of any two daily hours during which forty or more school pedestrians cross while going to or from school, or\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EIn rural areas where the vehicular traffic volume exceeds three hundred in each of any two daily hours during which thirty or more school pedestrians cross while going to or from school. Whenever the critical approach speed exceeds forty miles per hour, the warrants for rural areas should be applied;\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EAt stop sign controlled crossings: Where the vehicular traffic volume on undivided highways of four or more lanes exceeds five hundred per hour during any period when the school pedestrians are going to or from school;\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EAt traffic signal-controlled crossings:\u003Col\u003E\u003Cli\u003EWhere the number of vehicular turning movements through the school crosswalk exceeds three hundred per hour while school pedestrians are going to or from school,\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EWhere there are circumstances not normally present at a signalized intersection, such as crosswalks more than eighty feet long with no intermediate refuge, or any abnormally high proportion of large commercial vehicles.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1417, (part), 1987)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"56469d99-7a5d-4d12-9cff-518623d0bc23","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/ecb3b263-7de7-4f52-a7d4-ff7a28eb9ae7\/73f5bb64-e9eb-4dd7-85c2-86adfae1c6b1","ref":{"parent":"ecb3b263-7de7-4f52-a7d4-ff7a28eb9ae7","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-14-15","docId":"75","text":"11.09.060 Obedience to Adult Crossing Guards.","id":"73f5bb64-e9eb-4dd7-85c2-86adfae1c6b1","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/ecb3b263-7de7-4f52-a7d4-ff7a28eb9ae7\/73f5bb64-e9eb-4dd7-85c2-86adfae1c6b1\/9f038d11-bf72-473b-82ec-ed8f5da36d40","ref":{"parent":"73f5bb64-e9eb-4dd7-85c2-86adfae1c6b1","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-14-15-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EIt is unlawful for any person to disobey the traffic directions of a person appointed or authorized by the City to regulate traffic pursuant to Section 11.09.050 when such appointee is wearing an official insignia issued by the City and is acting in the course of his\/her appointed duty.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1417, (part), 1987)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"9f038d11-bf72-473b-82ec-ed8f5da36d40","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/ecb3b263-7de7-4f52-a7d4-ff7a28eb9ae7\/b7110c68-80da-46e3-90da-bcc5c542205d","ref":{"parent":"ecb3b263-7de7-4f52-a7d4-ff7a28eb9ae7","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-14-16","docId":"75","text":"11.09.090 Violation\u2013Penalty.","id":"b7110c68-80da-46e3-90da-bcc5c542205d","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/ecb3b263-7de7-4f52-a7d4-ff7a28eb9ae7\/b7110c68-80da-46e3-90da-bcc5c542205d\/57d5d6fe-c993-4d0e-bad0-ee3ead8f5117","ref":{"parent":"b7110c68-80da-46e3-90da-bcc5c542205d","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-14-16-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EAny person, firm or corporation violating any provision of this chapter shall be deemed guilty of an infraction, and upon conviction thereof, shall be punished as provided in Chapter 1.12 of this code.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1417, (part), 1987)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"57d5d6fe-c993-4d0e-bad0-ee3ead8f5117","prev_id":null}]}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/e0365f59-85b1-4631-bc04-8300481f5d2b","ref":{"parent":"ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":1,"tag":"h3"},"pos":"212-15","docId":"75","text":"CHAPTER 11.10: OFF-STREET VEHICLES","id":"e0365f59-85b1-4631-bc04-8300481f5d2b","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/e0365f59-85b1-4631-bc04-8300481f5d2b\/89c75851-5952-4106-83b1-8031e829631f","ref":{"parent":"e0365f59-85b1-4631-bc04-8300481f5d2b","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-15-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"89c75851-5952-4106-83b1-8031e829631f","prev_id":null},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/e0365f59-85b1-4631-bc04-8300481f5d2b\/95da60bc-1081-4b30-8e3d-18b54d2169da","ref":{"parent":"e0365f59-85b1-4631-bc04-8300481f5d2b","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-15-12","docId":"75","text":"11.10.010 Purpose.","id":"95da60bc-1081-4b30-8e3d-18b54d2169da","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/e0365f59-85b1-4631-bc04-8300481f5d2b\/95da60bc-1081-4b30-8e3d-18b54d2169da\/cda350c9-9ec2-44c0-bde1-6ee8f60f4f0d","ref":{"parent":"95da60bc-1081-4b30-8e3d-18b54d2169da","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-15-12-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EThe City Council finds that certain off-street operation of vehicles creates unnecessary, excessive and annoying noise, dust and fumes, and exposes both private and public property to the dangers of fire and soil erosion, any of which adversely affect the public peace, health, welfare and safety and all of which shall be regulated for the protection of the public.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1322, (part), 1985)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"cda350c9-9ec2-44c0-bde1-6ee8f60f4f0d","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/e0365f59-85b1-4631-bc04-8300481f5d2b\/c2e02bcf-d1f7-4590-bd48-e6a17d0690ea","ref":{"parent":"e0365f59-85b1-4631-bc04-8300481f5d2b","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-15-13","docId":"75","text":"11.10.011 Definition.","id":"c2e02bcf-d1f7-4590-bd48-e6a17d0690ea","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/e0365f59-85b1-4631-bc04-8300481f5d2b\/c2e02bcf-d1f7-4590-bd48-e6a17d0690ea\/23640c6b-c6a5-424f-a1fb-d5a5d8d78628","ref":{"parent":"c2e02bcf-d1f7-4590-bd48-e6a17d0690ea","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-15-13-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003E\u201cVehicle\u201d for the purpose of this chapter is a device by which any person or property may be propelled, moved or drawn, excepting a device moved by human power. \u201cVehicle\u201d includes, but is not limited to, automobile, motorcycle, RV, ATV, ATC, motor drive cycle, four-wheel drive and motor vehicle as defined in the Vehicle Code of the state of California.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1322, (part), 1985)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"23640c6b-c6a5-424f-a1fb-d5a5d8d78628","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/e0365f59-85b1-4631-bc04-8300481f5d2b\/09ac3dc9-5678-4aec-9157-f11e4b674f69","ref":{"parent":"e0365f59-85b1-4631-bc04-8300481f5d2b","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-15-14","docId":"75","text":"11.10.012 Regulation.","id":"09ac3dc9-5678-4aec-9157-f11e4b674f69","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/e0365f59-85b1-4631-bc04-8300481f5d2b\/09ac3dc9-5678-4aec-9157-f11e4b674f69\/3f9300a3-b126-4ec8-9e2a-27cc914e720f","ref":{"parent":"09ac3dc9-5678-4aec-9157-f11e4b674f69","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-15-14-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003ENo person shall operate a vehicle on private or public property in the City without first having obtained a permit. Permits shall be issued by the Chief of Police upon a determination that:\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Col class=\u0022default-style\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:upper-alpha\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe owner or owners of the residential property concerned, or the person or persons in possession thereof, have consented in writing to the proposed operation;\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe property concerned as shown on the latest Assessor\u2019s map is at least five hundred feet from any residence, church, school or place of assemblage which has not consented in writing to the proposed operation;\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe Director of Planning and Inspection has certified that the proposed operation conforms to the uses permitted on subject property by the City\u2019s zoning ordinance;\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe Fire Marshal has certified that the proposed operation will not create a fire hazard; and\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe Director of Public Works-City Engineer has certified that the proposed operation will not adversely affect public property.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe permit shall specify the area of permitted operation and period for which is valid. The permit shall further state that the City makes no representation as to safety of persons or property and that all risks are assumed by the applicant, property owner or other responsible person.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1322, (part), 1985)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"3f9300a3-b126-4ec8-9e2a-27cc914e720f","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/e0365f59-85b1-4631-bc04-8300481f5d2b\/fb047c23-02f0-4bc2-967b-b96916c334b0","ref":{"parent":"e0365f59-85b1-4631-bc04-8300481f5d2b","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-15-15","docId":"75","text":"11.10.013 Exemption from Regulation.","id":"fb047c23-02f0-4bc2-967b-b96916c334b0","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/e0365f59-85b1-4631-bc04-8300481f5d2b\/fb047c23-02f0-4bc2-967b-b96916c334b0\/28fdb989-713b-44d8-9b02-182256b95d41","ref":{"parent":"fb047c23-02f0-4bc2-967b-b96916c334b0","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-15-15-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EExempt from the regulation of this Article are:\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Col class=\u0022default-style\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:upper-alpha\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003EOperation under the state of California Vehicle Code of vehicles having valid registration driven by persons possessing valid operators\u2019 license upon the public streets and highways and for normal ingress and egress from private and public property where driveways and parking places are used in a reasonable and customary manner.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EVehicles designed primarily for agricultural, horticultural or construction purposes and used in the ordinary lawful way in such activities.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EOperation of publicly owned vehicles by a public employee acting within the course and scope of his employment.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EOperation of vehicles on private vehicular rights of way by those having ownership thereof or an easement or license to do so.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1322, (part), 1985)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"28fdb989-713b-44d8-9b02-182256b95d41","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/e0365f59-85b1-4631-bc04-8300481f5d2b\/7c379ed6-bc90-474e-975c-c2ffd590fcfd","ref":{"parent":"e0365f59-85b1-4631-bc04-8300481f5d2b","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-15-16","docId":"75","text":"11.10.014 Responsibility of Parents and Guardians.","id":"7c379ed6-bc90-474e-975c-c2ffd590fcfd","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/e0365f59-85b1-4631-bc04-8300481f5d2b\/7c379ed6-bc90-474e-975c-c2ffd590fcfd\/9f883e0f-398a-4b2c-a75b-787e68b5432f","ref":{"parent":"7c379ed6-bc90-474e-975c-c2ffd590fcfd","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-15-16-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003ENo parent, guardian or other adult person having control, custody or care of any minor under the age of eighteen years shall permit, allow or let such minor to violate any provision of this chapter.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1322, (part), 1985)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"9f883e0f-398a-4b2c-a75b-787e68b5432f","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/e0365f59-85b1-4631-bc04-8300481f5d2b\/95a48b10-0e52-40d6-94d2-a79a8c3561c6","ref":{"parent":"e0365f59-85b1-4631-bc04-8300481f5d2b","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-15-17","docId":"75","text":"11.10.015 Appeal.","id":"95a48b10-0e52-40d6-94d2-a79a8c3561c6","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/e0365f59-85b1-4631-bc04-8300481f5d2b\/95a48b10-0e52-40d6-94d2-a79a8c3561c6\/c9c2d5d7-5856-4d76-8192-ac2ea7d37afa","ref":{"parent":"95a48b10-0e52-40d6-94d2-a79a8c3561c6","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-15-17-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EAny person whose application for a permit is denied may appeal such decision to the City Council by filing a written notice of appeal within ten days after notification by the Chief of Police that such permit has been denied. The City Council shall thereupon conduct a hearing on said appeal within thirty days from the date of filing such notice of appeal with the City Clerk. The decision of the City Council shall be final and conclusive upon all persons concerned.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1322, (part), 1985)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"c9c2d5d7-5856-4d76-8192-ac2ea7d37afa","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/e0365f59-85b1-4631-bc04-8300481f5d2b\/08a43fa9-c49a-4f5b-8e48-ac2c2b3d5bbd","ref":{"parent":"e0365f59-85b1-4631-bc04-8300481f5d2b","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-15-18","docId":"75","text":"11.10.016 Penalty.","id":"08a43fa9-c49a-4f5b-8e48-ac2c2b3d5bbd","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/e0365f59-85b1-4631-bc04-8300481f5d2b\/08a43fa9-c49a-4f5b-8e48-ac2c2b3d5bbd\/594cfa9b-f32b-4551-a1e2-b89e28a91de0","ref":{"parent":"08a43fa9-c49a-4f5b-8e48-ac2c2b3d5bbd","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-15-18-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EAny person who violates any of the provisions of this chapter shall be guilty of an infraction and upon conviction thereof shall be punished as provided in Chapter 1.12 of this code.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1731, (part), 1996; Ord. 1322, (part), 1985)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"594cfa9b-f32b-4551-a1e2-b89e28a91de0","prev_id":null}]}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/264dce20-4f57-4b99-931c-4f793c0b4dea","ref":{"parent":"ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":1,"tag":"h3"},"pos":"212-16","docId":"75","text":"CHAPTER 11.12: SPEED LIMITS","id":"264dce20-4f57-4b99-931c-4f793c0b4dea","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/264dce20-4f57-4b99-931c-4f793c0b4dea\/5bef20a6-8b35-49b0-9087-e45ba991848b","ref":{"parent":"264dce20-4f57-4b99-931c-4f793c0b4dea","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-16-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"5bef20a6-8b35-49b0-9087-e45ba991848b","prev_id":null},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/264dce20-4f57-4b99-931c-4f793c0b4dea\/c4289ca1-c192-45d2-b7e7-319b353d990b","ref":{"parent":"264dce20-4f57-4b99-931c-4f793c0b4dea","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-16-12","docId":"75","text":"11.12.010 Purpose.","id":"c4289ca1-c192-45d2-b7e7-319b353d990b","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/264dce20-4f57-4b99-931c-4f793c0b4dea\/c4289ca1-c192-45d2-b7e7-319b353d990b\/946b999a-3d95-4ee5-8382-31c3cd8d380d","ref":{"parent":"c4289ca1-c192-45d2-b7e7-319b353d990b","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-16-12-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EIt is the express purpose of the ordinance codified in this chapter to consolidate in one ordinance all speed limits established pursuant to authority contained in the California Vehicle Code Sections 22357 and 22358, upon streets or highways presently or hereafter within the City limits, and to provide a means for incorporating therein all the speed limits that may hereafter be so established.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 490, \u00a7 1, 1971)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"946b999a-3d95-4ee5-8382-31c3cd8d380d","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/264dce20-4f57-4b99-931c-4f793c0b4dea\/d8f114e0-e8bd-4d1e-afac-b26950ad71b4","ref":{"parent":"264dce20-4f57-4b99-931c-4f793c0b4dea","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-16-13","docId":"75","text":"11.12.020 Definition.","id":"d8f114e0-e8bd-4d1e-afac-b26950ad71b4","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/264dce20-4f57-4b99-931c-4f793c0b4dea\/d8f114e0-e8bd-4d1e-afac-b26950ad71b4\/b5485296-5c26-4d6a-84f6-3b41db73fcfe","ref":{"parent":"d8f114e0-e8bd-4d1e-afac-b26950ad71b4","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-16-13-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EPursuant to authority contained in the California Vehicle Code, it is determined upon the basis of an engineering and traffic survey that a speed greater or lesser than that permitted by state law as applicable upon the following streets would facilitate the orderly movement of vehicular traffic and would be reasonable and safe under the conditions found to exist upon such streets, and it is declared that the prima facie speed limit shall be as hereinafter set forth on those streets or parts of streets herein designated when signs are erected giving notice thereof.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 490, \u00a7 2, 1971)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"b5485296-5c26-4d6a-84f6-3b41db73fcfe","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/264dce20-4f57-4b99-931c-4f793c0b4dea\/61249500-32ca-41f5-8ee0-ff65d94ddfdf","ref":{"parent":"264dce20-4f57-4b99-931c-4f793c0b4dea","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-16-14","docId":"75","text":"11.12.030 Establishment of Prima Facie Speed Limits.","id":"61249500-32ca-41f5-8ee0-ff65d94ddfdf","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/264dce20-4f57-4b99-931c-4f793c0b4dea\/61249500-32ca-41f5-8ee0-ff65d94ddfdf\/1afcbd3e-487e-4f72-9a5e-538a6bbb0bab","ref":{"parent":"61249500-32ca-41f5-8ee0-ff65d94ddfdf","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-16-14-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EThe prima facie speed limits on certain streets or highways, situated within the City of Cupertino, State of California shall be as set forth in Table 11.12.030.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1731, (part), 1996; Ord. 1692, 1995; Ord. 1584, 1992; Ord. 1579, 1992; Ord. 1566, 1991; Ord. 1556, 1991: Ord. 1548, 1991; Ord. 1542, 1990; Ord. 1507, 1989; Ord. 1243, 1983; Ord. 1067, \u00a7 1, 1980; Ord. 1023 \u00a7 1, 1980; Ord. 955, \u00a7 1, 1979; Ord. 945, \u00a7 1, 1979; Ord. 939, \u00a7 1, 1979; Ord. 915, (part), 1979; Ord. 490, \u00a7 4, 1971)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"1afcbd3e-487e-4f72-9a5e-538a6bbb0bab","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/264dce20-4f57-4b99-931c-4f793c0b4dea\/68d9e014-f856-4a78-9b8f-28f0b9b7fff2","ref":{"parent":"264dce20-4f57-4b99-931c-4f793c0b4dea","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-16-15","docId":"75","text":"11.12.040 Speed Limit Signs.","id":"68d9e014-f856-4a78-9b8f-28f0b9b7fff2","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/264dce20-4f57-4b99-931c-4f793c0b4dea\/68d9e014-f856-4a78-9b8f-28f0b9b7fff2\/e8038c31-a4bf-4818-93e8-8dfc4041d26b","ref":{"parent":"68d9e014-f856-4a78-9b8f-28f0b9b7fff2","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-16-15-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EThe City Manager is instructed to have a standard type of speed limit sign installed at each applicable intersection of the street or highway enumerated in Section 11.12.030.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 915, (part), 1979; Ord. 490, \u00a7 5, 1971)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"e8038c31-a4bf-4818-93e8-8dfc4041d26b","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/264dce20-4f57-4b99-931c-4f793c0b4dea\/9eb16031-09c0-45da-847d-2b6751cb5fd2","ref":{"parent":"264dce20-4f57-4b99-931c-4f793c0b4dea","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-16-16","docId":"75","text":"TABLE 11.12.030","id":"9eb16031-09c0-45da-847d-2b6751cb5fd2","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/264dce20-4f57-4b99-931c-4f793c0b4dea\/9eb16031-09c0-45da-847d-2b6751cb5fd2\/52f854ba-9ef9-498a-8613-68ceaafd0c47","ref":{"parent":"9eb16031-09c0-45da-847d-2b6751cb5fd2","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-16-16-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Ctable style=\u0022width:600px\u0022\u003E\u003Cthead\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Cth scope=\u0022col\u0022\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003ENAME OF STREET OR PORTION AFFECTED\u003C\/strong\u003E\u003C\/th\u003E\u003Cth scope=\u0022col\u0022\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EDECLARED PRIMA FACIE SPEED LIMIT (Miles per Hour)\u003C\/strong\u003E\u003C\/th\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003C\/thead\u003E\u003Ctbody\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EBandley Drive situated between Alves Drive and Valley Green Drive\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E30\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EBandley Drive situated between Stevens Creek Boulevard and Alves Drive\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E25\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EBlaney Avenue presently or hereafter within the City of Cupertino, and situated between Bollinger Road and Beekman Place\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E30\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EBlaney Avenue situated between Beekman Place and Homestead Road\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E35\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EBollinger Road presently or hereafter within the City of Cupertino, and situated between De Anza Boulevard and the easterly City limits\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E35\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EBollinger Road west of De Anza Boulevard\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E30\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EBubb Road presently or hereafter within the City of Cupertino, and situated between Rainbow Drive and McClellan Road\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E30\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EBubb Road situated between McClellan Road and Stevens Creek Boulevard\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E35\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003ECristo Rey Drive within the City limits and between Foothill Boulevard and the west City limits\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E30\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EDe Anza Boulevard situated between Bollinger Road and a point 700 feet north of Homestead Road\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E40\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EFinch Avenue - Stevens Creek Boulevard to Vallco Parkway\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E35\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EFoothill Boulevard presently or hereafter within the City of Cupertino, and situated between McClellan Road and Stevens Creek Boulevard\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E30\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EFoothill Boulevard presently or hereafter within the City of Cupertino, and situated between Stevens Creek Boulevard and Junipero Serra Freeway\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E40\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EHomestead Road presently or hereafter within the City of Cupertino, and situated between Foothill Boulevard and a point 850 feet, more or less, east of Tantau Avenue\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E35\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EMary Avenue situated between Stevens Creek Boulevard and Meteor Drive\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E35\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EMcClellan Road presently or hereafter within the City of Cupertino, and situated between De Anza Boulevard and Bubb Road\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E30\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EMcClellan Road situated between Bubb Road and Foothill Boulevard\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E25\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EMiller Avenue situated between Stevens Creek Boulevard and Bollinger Road\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E35\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EProspect Road situated between Saratoga-Sunnyvale Road and Stelling Road\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E30\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\