\u003Cth scope=\u0022col\u0022\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EExceptions\u003C\/strong\u003E\u003C\/th\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003C\/thead\u003E\u003Ctbody\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EBonny Drive\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E30\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E8:00 a.m.-3:30 p.m., M-F\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EBoth\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EBetween Scofield Drive and Shelly Drive\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EWhen school is not in session\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EFinch Avenue\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E120\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E8 a.m. to 5 p.m.\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EWest\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EBetween Craft Drive and a point 300 feet south of Sorenson Avenue\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003ESundays and Holidays\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EFoothill Boulevard\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E15\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E10 a.m. to 5 p.m.\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EEast\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EBetween a point 320 feet north of Salem Avenue to a point 490 feet north of Salem Avenue\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003ENone\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EMary Avenue\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E180\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E8 a.m. to 5 p.m.\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EEast\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EBetween Senior Center Driveway to a point approximately 225 feet north thereof\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EWeekends and Holidays\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EImperial Avenue\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E30\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E8 a.m. to 3:30 p.m., M-F\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EBoth\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EFrom McClellan Road to a point 400 feet north thereof\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EWhen school is not in session\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EOrange Avenue\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E30\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E8 a.m. to 4 p.m., M-F\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EBoth\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EFrom McClellan Road to Dolores Avenue\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EWhen school is not in session\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EPepper Tree Lane\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E30\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E8:00 a.m.-3:30 p.m., M-F\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EBoth\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EBetween Stelling Road and Bonny Drive\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EWhen school is not in session\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003ERollingdell Drive\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E30\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EAll Hours\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003ENorth\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EBetween a point 310 feet from the west face-of-curb of De Anza Boulevard to a point 350 feet west thereof.\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003ENone\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EScofield Drive\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E30\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E8:00 a.m.-3:30 p.m., M-F\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EBoth\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EBetween Barbara land and Western Drive\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EWhen school is not in session\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003ETorre Avenue\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E20\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m.\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EEast\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EBetween a point 725 feet north of Pacifica Drive to a point 680 feet north of Pacifica Drive\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003ESaturdays, Sundays, and Holidays\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd\u003ETorre Avenue\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E120\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003E8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m.\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EEast\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003EBetween a point 680 feet north of Pacifica Drive to a point 400 feet north of Pacifica Drive\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd\u003ESaturdays, Sundays, and Holidays\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003C\/tbody\u003E\u003C\/table\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"db476492-1693-4cf7-a781-32b59814edb9","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/768def6a-9047-4624-a01e-bd6b29396fd0\/6dc46223-2351-4f53-861b-846da64092f7","ref":{"parent":"768def6a-9047-4624-a01e-bd6b29396fd0","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-18-221","docId":"75","text":"11.24.170 Limitations on Certain Streets.","id":"6dc46223-2351-4f53-861b-846da64092f7","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/768def6a-9047-4624-a01e-bd6b29396fd0\/6dc46223-2351-4f53-861b-846da64092f7\/7c5ec410-34c2-42ab-932d-3ff3244a82da","ref":{"parent":"6dc46223-2351-4f53-861b-846da64092f7","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-18-221-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003ENo person shall stop, stand, or park any vehicle as defined in the Vehicle Code of California, or as hereafter amended, on the streets or portions of streets, set out in Table 11.24.170, within the City for a period of time longer than that indicated opposite the name of each street between the respective hours set opposite the name of each street on any day, or on any one day and the next ensuing day, except as provided in this section.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 2002, 2007; Ord. 1930, 2004; Ord. 1914, (part), 2003; Ord. 1884, 2001; Ord. 1882, 2001; Ord. 1857, (part), 2000; Ord. 1476, (part), 1988; Ord. 1419, (part), 1987; Ord. 1409, (part), 1987; Ord. 1405, (part), 1987; Ord. 1276, (part), 1984; Ord. 1163, 1982; Ord. 843, \u00a7 10.3, 1977; Ord. 1991, 2006)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"7c5ec410-34c2-42ab-932d-3ff3244a82da","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/768def6a-9047-4624-a01e-bd6b29396fd0\/52abc5cd-db52-4cf4-83ab-c435ab0fde0a","ref":{"parent":"768def6a-9047-4624-a01e-bd6b29396fd0","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-18-222","docId":"75","text":"11.24.180 Diagonal Parking.","id":"52abc5cd-db52-4cf4-83ab-c435ab0fde0a","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/768def6a-9047-4624-a01e-bd6b29396fd0\/52abc5cd-db52-4cf4-83ab-c435ab0fde0a\/3a90f01a-61a2-4c5d-8187-0dcb417c4adf","ref":{"parent":"52abc5cd-db52-4cf4-83ab-c435ab0fde0a","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-18-222-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EDiagonal parking permitted on certain streets. No person shall stop, stand, or park any vehicle as defined in the Vehicle Code of California except within the parking stalls provided, marked and delineated on the following named streets:\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Ctable cellpadding=\u00220\u0022 cellspacing=\u00220\u0022 style=\u0022width:800px\u0022\u003E\u003Cthead\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Cth scope=\u0022col\u0022 style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EStreet\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/th\u003E\u003Cth scope=\u0022col\u0022 style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EPortion\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/th\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003C\/thead\u003E\u003Ctbody\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EImperial Avenue\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBetween Stevens Creek Boulevard and Granada Avenue\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EMary Avenue\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EWest side between a point 500 feet north of Stevens Creek Boulevard to a point 380 feet south of Lubec Street\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EMary Avenue\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EWest side between a point 430 feet north of Lubec Street and a point 340 feet northerly\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EMary Avenue\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBetween Homestead Road and a point 650 feet southerly thereof\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EPasadena Avenue\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBetween Stevens Creek Boulevard and Granada Avenue\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003ERichwood Court\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBetween Miller Avenue and the easterly terminus thereof\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003ERosemarie Place\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBetween Miller Avenue and the easterly terminus thereof\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003C\/tbody\u003E\u003C\/table\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1840, (part), 1999; Ord. 1483, 1989; Ord. 1348, 1986; Ord. 1340, 1985; Ord. 843, \u00a7 10.4, 1977)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"3a90f01a-61a2-4c5d-8187-0dcb417c4adf","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/768def6a-9047-4624-a01e-bd6b29396fd0\/d4498d99-15fc-456b-95f3-f7767e527e9f","ref":{"parent":"768def6a-9047-4624-a01e-bd6b29396fd0","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-18-223","docId":"75","text":"11.24.190 Off-street Parking for Handicapped Persons.","id":"d4498d99-15fc-456b-95f3-f7767e527e9f","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/768def6a-9047-4624-a01e-bd6b29396fd0\/d4498d99-15fc-456b-95f3-f7767e527e9f\/32c2f184-ac45-4124-8b22-38c5e81b5dc1","ref":{"parent":"d4498d99-15fc-456b-95f3-f7767e527e9f","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-18-223-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Col class=\u0022default-style\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:upper-alpha\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003EProperty Owned or Operated by the City. The City Traffic Engineer may designate stalls or spaces in any off-street parking facility owned or operated by the City for the exclusive use of vehicles which display a distinguishing license plate or placard issued by the California Department of Motor Vehicles to handicapped persons or to disabled veterans pursuant to Sections 22511.5 and 9105 of the California Vehicle Code. All spaces or stalls so designated shall be marked by posting immediately adjacent to, and visible from, each stall or space, a sign consisting of a profile view of a wheelchair with occupant in white on a blue background.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003ERemoval of Unauthorized Vehicles. The City may cause the removal, from a stall or space designated for physically handicapped persons in a parking facility owned or operated by the City, of any vehicle not displaying one of the distinguishing placards or license plates specified in Sections 22511.5 and 9105 of the California Vehicle Code if a sign is posted in conformance with Section 22511.8 of the California Vehicle Code which clearly and conspicuously gives the notice specified in that section.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe provisions of this section shall not be construed to restrict the rights of private property owners to designate parking areas for the exclusive use of handicapped persons under the provisions of Sections 22511.7 and 22511.8 of the California Vehicle Code.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 843, \u00a7 11, 1977)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"32c2f184-ac45-4124-8b22-38c5e81b5dc1","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/768def6a-9047-4624-a01e-bd6b29396fd0\/1958de8c-4766-4a6d-b585-e0139d07754e","ref":{"parent":"768def6a-9047-4624-a01e-bd6b29396fd0","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-18-224","docId":"75","text":"11.24.200 Removal of Vehicles from Street.","id":"1958de8c-4766-4a6d-b585-e0139d07754e","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/768def6a-9047-4624-a01e-bd6b29396fd0\/1958de8c-4766-4a6d-b585-e0139d07754e\/2d0c8ed0-7dec-422c-96d4-19e0fd700e94","ref":{"parent":"1958de8c-4766-4a6d-b585-e0139d07754e","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-18-224-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EAny regularly employed and salaried employee who is engaged in the direction of traffic or enforcement of parking regulations when designated by the sheriff may remove a vehicle from a street, except a freeway, in the manner and subject to the requirements of Vehicle Code of the state Sections 22650 through 22856 under the following circumstances:\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Col class=\u0022default-style\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:upper-alpha\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003EWhen any vehicle is illegally parked so as to block the entrance to a private driveway and it is impractical to move such vehicle from in front of the driveway to another point on the street;\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EWhen any vehicle is illegally parked so as to prevent access by firefighting equipment to a fire hydrant and it is impracticable to move such vehicle from in front of the fire hydrant to another point on the street;\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EWhen a vehicle is parked or left standing upon a highway for seventy-two or more consecutive hours;\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EWhen a vehicle is parked or left standing upon a street where the use of such street or a portion thereof is necessary for the cleaning, repair or construction of the street, or for the installation of underground utilities, or where the use of the street or any portion thereof is authorized for a purpose other than the normal flow of traffic, or where the use of the street or any portion thereof is necessary for the movement of equipment, articles or structures of unusual size, and the parking of such vehicle would prohibit or interfere with such use or movement; provided, that signs giving notice that such vehicle may be removed are erected or placed at least twenty-four hours prior to removal;\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EWhen a vehicle is parked or left standing on a highway so as to obstruct the normal movement of traffic;\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EWhen any vehicle is found illegally parked and there are no license plates or other evidence of registration displayed, the vehicle may be impounded until the owner or person in control of the vehicle furnishes evidence of his or her identity and an address within California at which he or she can be located;\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EWhenever any vehicle is parked or left standing where parking is prohibited by ordinance and signs are posted giving notice of authorization for removal.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1500, \u00a7\u00a7 1, 2, 1989; Ord. 843, \u00a7 7, 1977)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"2d0c8ed0-7dec-422c-96d4-19e0fd700e94","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/768def6a-9047-4624-a01e-bd6b29396fd0\/82c1d130-bd21-413f-b984-70b8259ee77f","ref":{"parent":"768def6a-9047-4624-a01e-bd6b29396fd0","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-18-225","docId":"75","text":"11.24.210 Violation\u2013Penalty.","id":"82c1d130-bd21-413f-b984-70b8259ee77f","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/768def6a-9047-4624-a01e-bd6b29396fd0\/82c1d130-bd21-413f-b984-70b8259ee77f\/a6ea7422-e19d-4b34-a27f-9e1160f8fa28","ref":{"parent":"82c1d130-bd21-413f-b984-70b8259ee77f","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-18-225-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EAny person, firm or corporation violating any provision of this chapter shall be deemed guilty of an infraction, and, upon conviction thereof, shall be punished as provided in Chapter 1.12 of this Code.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 865, \u00a7 1, 1978; Ord. 843, \u00a7 12, 1977)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"a6ea7422-e19d-4b34-a27f-9e1160f8fa28","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/768def6a-9047-4624-a01e-bd6b29396fd0\/45810052-3205-4ac4-9712-84a0184e72f1","ref":{"parent":"768def6a-9047-4624-a01e-bd6b29396fd0","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-18-226","docId":"75","text":"11.24.220 Temporary Parking Zones\u2013Permit Procedure.","id":"45810052-3205-4ac4-9712-84a0184e72f1","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/768def6a-9047-4624-a01e-bd6b29396fd0\/45810052-3205-4ac4-9712-84a0184e72f1\/9618b041-502f-4ebf-b30d-a00f72c2e61d","ref":{"parent":"45810052-3205-4ac4-9712-84a0184e72f1","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-18-226-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Col class=\u0022default-style\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:upper-alpha\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThere is conferred upon the City Manager of the City of Cupertino those powers and duties necessary for the administration of this section. In addition, there is also conferred upon the City Manager the authority to designate such officers and employees of the City, as may be required, to assist him in carrying out the intent and purpose of this section. The person so designated by the City Manager is referred to in this section as the \u201cHearing Officer.\u201d\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe Hearing Officer may designate any area to be a temporary parking zone, upon compliance with the application procedure specified in this section, if in his discretion the public benefits of such a designation will outweigh the particular harm caused to affected persons or properties. The size and duration of said zone shall be designed in a manner reasonably limiting any harmful consequences.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EA temporary parking zone shall be indicated by such appropriate signs, sign covers, or markings as the Hearing Officer may specify. Said signs shall notify the public of the existence of a temporary parking zone, the applicant\u2019s permit number, and of any special provisions designated by the Hearing Officer. The duration of the existence of said zone shall be indicated on the appropriate signs, and unless pursuant to a renewal of the original application, shall not exceed twenty days.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EWithin the area designated as a temporary parking zone, the special provisions indicated on the appropriate signs shall supersede all other parking ordinances and regulations inconsistent therewith, during the time periods indicated on said signs.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EAny person residing upon or conducting a business upon a parcel of real property within the city limits of the City of Cupertino, may apply to the Hearing Officer for a permit designating a temporary parking zone to exist in the area immediately adjacent to said parcel of real property. Said application shall be made according to the following procedure:\u003Col\u003E\u003Cli\u003EAn applicant shall submit an application for a temporary parking zone permit to the office of the City Manager a minimum of ten days before the intended designation, containing the following items:\u003Col class=\u0022default-style\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:lower-alpha\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003EApplicant\u2019s name and name of business, if appropriate;\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EApplicant\u2019s telephone number;\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EApplicant\u2019s address;\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EArea to be designated temporary parking zone;\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EDates and duration of permit, not to exceed twenty days;\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003ESpecial provisions or limitations, if any;\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EA statement of the purpose and\/or special event necessitating the designation of a temporary parking zone;\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EA statement of the estimated harmful effects such designation might have upon persons or properties affected thereby;\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EA check in the amount of twenty-five dollars to cover processing and staff investigation costs;\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EA separate check in the amount of fifty dollars, comprising a deposit to insure against the loss of or damage to any signs, sign covers or markings designating said zone, from any cause. The deposit shall be refunded to applicant in the amount that it exceeds actual repair or replacement costs for said signs.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EUpon receipt of each complete application, the Hearing Officer shall assign a number to it, and review its contents and all relevant circumstances. The inception and termination dates of the zone, its extent, duration, and other special provisions all may be amended to conform to the public interest. As amended, the application may be marked \u201cpermitted\u201d or \u201cnot permitted,\u201d as appropriate. An application marked \u201cpermitted\u201d shall constitute a temporary parking zone permit. All applications shall be retained by the office of the City Manager in an appropriate file.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EIn the event that the date designated on the application for inception of the zone passes without approval or disapproval by the Hearing Officer, the application shall be deemed \u201cnot permitted,\u201d and the full amount of both the deposit and the processing fee shall be remitted to the applicant.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EIn the event that the application is disapproved before the desired inception date, the full amount of the deposit shall be remitted to the applicant.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EIn the event that the application is approved, the Hearing Officer shall notify the applicant and shall cause to be installed such appropriate signs, sign covers or markings as shall indicate the existence of the temporary parking zone in accordance with the terms of this section.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe Hearing Officer shall, within ten days following the termination of the zone, remove all of said signs. Upon receipt of a proper accounting for those damaged or lost, the Hearing Officer shall refund the proper amount described in subsection (1)(5).\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003ERenewal of a permit may be granted by the Hearing Officer upon receipt of a renewal request before termination of the zone, and upon a review of all relevant circumstances, in a manner consistent with the terms of this section.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EIn the event that an application is not approved, the applicant may request a public hearing of the matter at the next regularly scheduled meeting of the Cupertino City Council. The City Council, at such hearing, shall hear all relevant circumstances and determine whether the application should be approved.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThis section is intended to be construed broadly, to effect its purpose of temporarily superseding other parking ordinances and regulations of the City of Cupertino. This section is enacted pursuant to the authority granted by California Vehicle Code Sections 21100(d), 21101, and 21351, as amended, and in no event shall be construed so as to contravene that authority.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 903, (part), 1978)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"9618b041-502f-4ebf-b30d-a00f72c2e61d","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/768def6a-9047-4624-a01e-bd6b29396fd0\/8db0f605-6806-40b4-b86f-1a2bb7eb494b","ref":{"parent":"768def6a-9047-4624-a01e-bd6b29396fd0","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-18-227","docId":"75","text":"11.24.230 Parking Prohibited Where Use of Street Is Necessary for Cleaning or Repair.","id":"8db0f605-6806-40b4-b86f-1a2bb7eb494b","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/768def6a-9047-4624-a01e-bd6b29396fd0\/8db0f605-6806-40b4-b86f-1a2bb7eb494b\/7e3c3a90-a6e4-45d5-be0d-9ebec2ac6bee","ref":{"parent":"8db0f605-6806-40b4-b86f-1a2bb7eb494b","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-18-227-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Col class=\u0022default-style\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:upper-alpha\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003EWhenever the City Manager or his authorized representative finds and determines that the use of a street or highway, or portion thereof, in the City is necessary for the cleaning or repair of the highway or street, and that the parking or standing of vehicles hereon would prohibit or interfere with such cleaning or repair, he is authorized to erect or place signs, or have signs erected or placed, on such street, highway or portion, in the manner required and subject to the requirements of the Vehicle Code of the State, giving notice that the parking or standing of vehicles upon such street, highway or portion is forbidden, and keep such signs thereon until such cleaning or repair is completed.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EUpon and after the erection or placing of such signs thereon and until such signs are removed, no person who owns or has possession, custody or control of any vehicle shall park such vehicle standing upon the street or highway or portion thereof upon which such signs are erected or placed.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1408, \u00a7 1, 1987)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"7e3c3a90-a6e4-45d5-be0d-9ebec2ac6bee","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/768def6a-9047-4624-a01e-bd6b29396fd0\/1457d767-0667-469f-a5f0-1e3a7f06a290","ref":{"parent":"768def6a-9047-4624-a01e-bd6b29396fd0","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-18-228","docId":"75","text":"11.24.240 Blocking of Intersections Prohibited.","id":"1457d767-0667-469f-a5f0-1e3a7f06a290","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/768def6a-9047-4624-a01e-bd6b29396fd0\/1457d767-0667-469f-a5f0-1e3a7f06a290\/c7d60bc2-b0c5-4b68-adf8-b5427939b983","ref":{"parent":"1457d767-0667-469f-a5f0-1e3a7f06a290","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-18-228-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EIt is unlawful for any vehicle to enter an intersection or a marked crosswalk where \u201cKeep Clear\u201d legends have been painted and signs have been posted, unless there is sufficient space on the other side of the intersection or crossing at the far side of the intersection to accommodate the vehicle without obstructing the passage of other vehicles or pedestrians, notwithstanding any traffic control signal device indication to proceed.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1416, 1987)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"c7d60bc2-b0c5-4b68-adf8-b5427939b983","prev_id":null}]}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f5669e6a-1ff3-4b85-99f5-ddcdd7865570","ref":{"parent":"ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":1,"tag":"h3"},"pos":"212-19","docId":"75","text":"CHAPTER 11.26: STOPPING, STANDING AND PARKING--PRIVATE STREETS","id":"f5669e6a-1ff3-4b85-99f5-ddcdd7865570","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f5669e6a-1ff3-4b85-99f5-ddcdd7865570\/259b14d9-db20-4fba-989c-e81ad9359644","ref":{"parent":"f5669e6a-1ff3-4b85-99f5-ddcdd7865570","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-19-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"259b14d9-db20-4fba-989c-e81ad9359644","prev_id":null},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f5669e6a-1ff3-4b85-99f5-ddcdd7865570\/a638ff96-22bc-4eff-95ad-6a29c52b3aee","ref":{"parent":"f5669e6a-1ff3-4b85-99f5-ddcdd7865570","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-19-12","docId":"75","text":"11.26.010 Purpose.","id":"a638ff96-22bc-4eff-95ad-6a29c52b3aee","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f5669e6a-1ff3-4b85-99f5-ddcdd7865570\/a638ff96-22bc-4eff-95ad-6a29c52b3aee\/ef2e577d-e26f-4995-b2e1-ba9286272402","ref":{"parent":"a638ff96-22bc-4eff-95ad-6a29c52b3aee","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-19-12-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EThe provisions of this chapter prohibiting the stopping, standing or parking of a vehicle shall apply at all times, or at those times herein specified, except when it is necessary either to stop a vehicle to avoid conflict with other traffic, or in compliance with the directions of a law enforcement officer or official traffic-control device.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 831, \u00a7 3.1, 1977)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"ef2e577d-e26f-4995-b2e1-ba9286272402","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f5669e6a-1ff3-4b85-99f5-ddcdd7865570\/a853a1ce-7cf6-459c-82cb-1f2db698586a","ref":{"parent":"f5669e6a-1ff3-4b85-99f5-ddcdd7865570","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-19-13","docId":"75","text":"11.26.020 Scope.","id":"a853a1ce-7cf6-459c-82cb-1f2db698586a","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f5669e6a-1ff3-4b85-99f5-ddcdd7865570\/a853a1ce-7cf6-459c-82cb-1f2db698586a\/14e83305-2082-4cd5-a1cd-91b99213d0e2","ref":{"parent":"a853a1ce-7cf6-459c-82cb-1f2db698586a","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-19-13-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EThe provisions of this chapter imposing a time limit on stopping, standing or parking shall not relieve any person from the duty to observe other and more restrictive provisions of the Vehicle Code of the state, or the ordinances of the City prohibiting or limiting the stopping, standing or parking of vehicles in specified places or at specified times.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 831, \u00a7 3.2, 1977)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"14e83305-2082-4cd5-a1cd-91b99213d0e2","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f5669e6a-1ff3-4b85-99f5-ddcdd7865570\/cab03838-1a28-428c-8d5c-86de6807f2a8","ref":{"parent":"f5669e6a-1ff3-4b85-99f5-ddcdd7865570","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-19-14","docId":"75","text":"11.26.030 Definitions.","id":"cab03838-1a28-428c-8d5c-86de6807f2a8","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f5669e6a-1ff3-4b85-99f5-ddcdd7865570\/cab03838-1a28-428c-8d5c-86de6807f2a8\/eda9a7ac-6d71-4131-b2f2-d069642bd8bc","ref":{"parent":"cab03838-1a28-428c-8d5c-86de6807f2a8","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-19-14-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EThe following words and phrases when used in this chapter shall have the meanings set forth in this section:\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Col class=\u0022default-style\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:upper-alpha\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u201cHighway\u201d means any private roadway upon which sections of the Vehicle Code have been made applicable by the City Council.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u201cHolidays\u201d are the first day in January, Memorial Day, Independence Day, Admission Day, Labor Day, Thanksgiving Day, and Christmas.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u201cIntersection\u201d means the area embraced within the prolongation of the lateral curb lines, or, if none, then the lateral boundary lines of the roadways, of two highways which join one another at approximately right angles, or the area within which vehicles traveling upon different highways joining at any other angle may come in conflict.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u201cPark\u201d means to stand or leave standing any vehicle, whether occupied or not, otherwise than temporarily for the purpose of and while actually engaged in loading or unloading of passengers or materials.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u201cParkway\u201d means that portion of a street other than a roadway or sidewalk.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u201cRoadway\u201d means that portion of a highway improved, designed, or ordinarily used for vehicular travel.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u201cSidewalk\u201d means that portion of a highway, other than the roadway, set apart by curbs, barriers, markings, or other delineation for pedestrian travel.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u201cStop\u201d or \u201cstopping\u201d when prohibited means any cessation of movement of a vehicle, whether occupied or not, except when necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic or in compliance with the direction of a police officer or official traffic-control device or signal.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u201cStreet\u201d means highway.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 831, \u00a7 1, 1977)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"eda9a7ac-6d71-4131-b2f2-d069642bd8bc","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f5669e6a-1ff3-4b85-99f5-ddcdd7865570\/08d1b88c-6035-4d39-bf19-85dc47ba3b3a","ref":{"parent":"f5669e6a-1ff3-4b85-99f5-ddcdd7865570","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-19-15","docId":"75","text":"11.26.040 Curb Markings and Signs Designated.","id":"08d1b88c-6035-4d39-bf19-85dc47ba3b3a","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f5669e6a-1ff3-4b85-99f5-ddcdd7865570\/08d1b88c-6035-4d39-bf19-85dc47ba3b3a\/19057305-a738-462b-9bd4-91e2205fcd6d","ref":{"parent":"08d1b88c-6035-4d39-bf19-85dc47ba3b3a","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-19-15-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EThe City Traffic Engineer is hereby authorized, subject to the provisions and limitations of this chapter, to approve, and when required herein shall approve, the following curb markings or curb markings and signs to indicate parking or standing regulations, and the curb markings shall have the meanings as set forth in this section.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Col class=\u0022default-style\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:upper-alpha\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003ENo Parking Zone. Red means no stopping, standing or parking at any time except as permitted by the Vehicle Code, except that a bus may stop in a red zone marked or signed as a bus zone.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003ELoading Zone. Yellow means no stopping, standing or parking for any purpose other than the loading or unloading of passengers or materials to and from commercial vehicles making commercial deliveries, provided, that the loading or unloading of passengers shall not consume more than three minutes, nor the loading or unloading of materials more than twenty minutes, unless the City Traffic Engineer has approved signs to be posted giving notice of a different period in which the restrictions shall apply.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EPassenger Loading Zone. White means no stopping, standing or parking for any purpose other than the loading or unloading of passengers, which shall not exceed three minutes, unless the City Traffic Engineer has approved signs to be posted giving notice of a different period in which the restrictions shall apply.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003ERestricted Parking Zone. Green means no stopping, standing or parking for longer than twelve minutes at any time between 7:00 a.m. and 6:00 p.m. on any day except Sundays and holidays, unless the City Traffic Engineer has approved signs, markings, or curb markings and signs to be posted giving notice of a different period in which the restrictions apply.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EHandicapped Parking Zone. Blue means no stopping, standing or parking except for vehicles of physically handicapped persons.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 831, \u00a7 2, 1977)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"19057305-a738-462b-9bd4-91e2205fcd6d","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f5669e6a-1ff3-4b85-99f5-ddcdd7865570\/ffa4cfc5-8388-41cd-883f-c249025e5f02","ref":{"parent":"f5669e6a-1ff3-4b85-99f5-ddcdd7865570","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-19-16","docId":"75","text":"11.26.050 Obedience to Signs.","id":"ffa4cfc5-8388-41cd-883f-c249025e5f02","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f5669e6a-1ff3-4b85-99f5-ddcdd7865570\/ffa4cfc5-8388-41cd-883f-c249025e5f02\/d6cf0abe-9ecb-4f2b-b741-2addebf12cd4","ref":{"parent":"ffa4cfc5-8388-41cd-883f-c249025e5f02","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-19-16-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EWhenever signs have been erected, pursuant to Section 11.26.040, no person shall stop, stand or park any vehicle in the area designated by such sign.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 831, \u00a7 4.1, 1977)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"d6cf0abe-9ecb-4f2b-b741-2addebf12cd4","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f5669e6a-1ff3-4b85-99f5-ddcdd7865570\/73e02640-a03d-4a1f-ad1a-162506cf6cc0","ref":{"parent":"f5669e6a-1ff3-4b85-99f5-ddcdd7865570","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-19-17","docId":"75","text":"11.26.060 Parking Space Markings.","id":"73e02640-a03d-4a1f-ad1a-162506cf6cc0","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f5669e6a-1ff3-4b85-99f5-ddcdd7865570\/73e02640-a03d-4a1f-ad1a-162506cf6cc0\/93dad7ac-c857-4173-8994-7acf6a00c941","ref":{"parent":"73e02640-a03d-4a1f-ad1a-162506cf6cc0","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-19-17-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EThe City Traffic Engineer is authorized to approve parking space markings to indicate parking spaces adjacent to curbings where authorized parking is permitted. When such parking space markings are placed in the highway, subject to other and more restrictive limitations, no vehicle shall be stopped, left standing or parked, other than within a single space, unless the size or shape of such vehicle makes compliance impossible.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 831, \u00a7 4.2, 1977)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"93dad7ac-c857-4173-8994-7acf6a00c941","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f5669e6a-1ff3-4b85-99f5-ddcdd7865570\/1b6258d5-5fdb-41ac-bc65-c429808ad5fa","ref":{"parent":"f5669e6a-1ff3-4b85-99f5-ddcdd7865570","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-19-18","docId":"75","text":"11.26.070 Authority to Establish Loading Zones.","id":"1b6258d5-5fdb-41ac-bc65-c429808ad5fa","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f5669e6a-1ff3-4b85-99f5-ddcdd7865570\/1b6258d5-5fdb-41ac-bc65-c429808ad5fa\/ba43dc21-6c3a-4528-ba27-492769546fc5","ref":{"parent":"1b6258d5-5fdb-41ac-bc65-c429808ad5fa","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-19-18-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EThe City Traffic Engineer is authorized to approve loading zones and passenger loading zones in front of any hall or place used for the purpose of public assembly.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 831, \u00a7 4.3, 1977)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"ba43dc21-6c3a-4528-ba27-492769546fc5","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f5669e6a-1ff3-4b85-99f5-ddcdd7865570\/644b8897-319e-48c3-ba2f-6159a502ccd8","ref":{"parent":"f5669e6a-1ff3-4b85-99f5-ddcdd7865570","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-19-19","docId":"75","text":"11.26.080 Loading Zones\u2013Marking.","id":"644b8897-319e-48c3-ba2f-6159a502ccd8","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f5669e6a-1ff3-4b85-99f5-ddcdd7865570\/644b8897-319e-48c3-ba2f-6159a502ccd8\/d7aea1ac-f2d7-48ae-8d83-634f4506edb6","ref":{"parent":"644b8897-319e-48c3-ba2f-6159a502ccd8","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-19-19-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003ELoading zones shall be indicated by a yellow paint line upon the top and face of all curbs within such zones.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 831, \u00a7 4.4, 1977)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"d7aea1ac-f2d7-48ae-8d83-634f4506edb6","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f5669e6a-1ff3-4b85-99f5-ddcdd7865570\/8a1380fe-593e-4cbb-9597-8e2c9004a550","ref":{"parent":"f5669e6a-1ff3-4b85-99f5-ddcdd7865570","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-19-210","docId":"75","text":"11.26.090 Passenger Loading Zones.","id":"8a1380fe-593e-4cbb-9597-8e2c9004a550","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f5669e6a-1ff3-4b85-99f5-ddcdd7865570\/8a1380fe-593e-4cbb-9597-8e2c9004a550\/c633a8f9-add7-4191-8cc8-8c90ebc91a18","ref":{"parent":"8a1380fe-593e-4cbb-9597-8e2c9004a550","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-19-210-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EPassenger loading zones shall be indicated by a white line stenciled with black letters \u201cPASSENGER LOADING ONLY\u201d upon the top of all curbs in said zones.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 831, \u00a7 4.5, 1977)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"c633a8f9-add7-4191-8cc8-8c90ebc91a18","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f5669e6a-1ff3-4b85-99f5-ddcdd7865570\/8114211f-9983-4f9b-80e2-3d945b781d6a","ref":{"parent":"f5669e6a-1ff3-4b85-99f5-ddcdd7865570","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-19-211","docId":"75","text":"11.26.100 Spaces Restricted to Handicapped Persons\u2013Markings.","id":"8114211f-9983-4f9b-80e2-3d945b781d6a","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f5669e6a-1ff3-4b85-99f5-ddcdd7865570\/8114211f-9983-4f9b-80e2-3d945b781d6a\/00bfce31-cdc0-479f-ae50-9dbba9802d67","ref":{"parent":"8114211f-9983-4f9b-80e2-3d945b781d6a","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-19-211-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EThe City Traffic Engineer is authorized to approve parking spaces for the exclusive use of vehicles which display a distinguishing license plate or placard issued by the California Department of Motor Vehicles to handicapped persons or to disabled veterans pursuant to Sections 22511.5 and 9105 of the California Vehicle Code.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EAll parking spaces so designated shall be identified by blue paint on the curb or edge of the paved portion of the street adjacent to the space. In addition to blue paint, the space may also be indicated by signs or other suitable means.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 831, \u00a7 4.6, 1977)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"00bfce31-cdc0-479f-ae50-9dbba9802d67","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f5669e6a-1ff3-4b85-99f5-ddcdd7865570\/dcd6fb1b-3ad9-4a97-aa70-a302840b60a8","ref":{"parent":"f5669e6a-1ff3-4b85-99f5-ddcdd7865570","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-19-212","docId":"75","text":"11.26.110 Parking Prohibited along Certain Streets.","id":"dcd6fb1b-3ad9-4a97-aa70-a302840b60a8","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f5669e6a-1ff3-4b85-99f5-ddcdd7865570\/dcd6fb1b-3ad9-4a97-aa70-a302840b60a8\/32fb8efe-48ee-44b7-9aca-2899025f0172","ref":{"parent":"dcd6fb1b-3ad9-4a97-aa70-a302840b60a8","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-19-212-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003ENo person shall stop, stand or park any vehicle as defined in the Vehicle Code of California on any day within the City:\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EA. On any of the following enumerated streets, or portions of streets within tract Nos. 5099, 5103, 5104, 5105, 5284, 5285, 5286 and 5287, Oak Meadows Subdivision:\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Ctable cellpadding=\u00220\u0022 cellspacing=\u00220\u0022 style=\u0022width:600px\u0022\u003E\u003Cthead\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Cth scope=\u0022col\u0022 style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EStreet\u003C\/strong\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/th\u003E\u003Cth scope=\u0022col\u0022 style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003ESides of Street\u003C\/strong\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/th\u003E\u003Cth scope=\u0022col\u0022 style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EPortion\u003C\/strong\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/th\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003C\/thead\u003E\u003Ctbody\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003ECamberley Lane\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBoth\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EAll\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003ECricket Hill Road\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBoth\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EAll\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EFirwood Drive\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EBoth\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C