03ETorre Avenue\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EEastside from Rodrigues Avenue to a point 265 feet southerly thereof\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EM--F 7:00 a.m.- 5:00 p.m., except holidays\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003ETula Court\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EAll\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EFirst Saturday of each month 8:00 a.m.--12:00 p.m.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003ETula Lane\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EAll\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EFirst Saturday of each month 8:00 a.m.--12:00 p.m.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EWhite Fir Court\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EAll\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EDaily, 8:00 a.m.-7:30 p.m.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EWilkinson Ave\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EHyannisport to Columbus\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EM--F 8:00 a.m.-- 3:30 p.m.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003C\/tbody\u003E\u003C\/table\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 21-2228, 2021; Ord. 18-2176, 2018; Ord. 17-2163, 2017; Ord. 16-2147, 2016; Ord. 16-2146, 2016; Ord. 16-2145, 2016; Ord. 14-2118, (part), 2014; Res. 03-037, 2011; Ord. 1989, 2006; Res. 99-154, 1999; Ord. 1731, (part), 1996; Ord. 24-2264, Att. A, 2024)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"447e43d0-2b68-4153-aaa1-4cc092415b19","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f40bcffd-181a-4ae9-8b03-473248efe7c5\/6bd5a744-414e-49ed-9906-f134a44774f6","ref":{"parent":"f40bcffd-181a-4ae9-8b03-473248efe7c5","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-210-217","docId":"75","text":"11.27.150 Penalty Provisions.","id":"6bd5a744-414e-49ed-9906-f134a44774f6","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f40bcffd-181a-4ae9-8b03-473248efe7c5\/6bd5a744-414e-49ed-9906-f134a44774f6\/8ac2cb19-fd5f-48fa-907e-3dabb70d879d","ref":{"parent":"6bd5a744-414e-49ed-9906-f134a44774f6","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-210-217-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Col class=\u0022default-style\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:upper-alpha\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003EIt is unlawful and a violation of this chapter for a person to falsely represent himself as eligible for a parking permit or to furnish false information in an application therefor to the Director of Public Works.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EIt is unlawful and a violation of this chapter for a person holding a valid parking permit issued pursuant hereto to knowingly permit the use or display of such permit on a motor vehicle other than that for which the permit is issued. Such conduct shall constitute an unlawful act and violation of this chapter both by the person holding the valid parking permit and the person who so uses or displays the permit on a motor vehicle other than that for which it is issued.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EIt is unlawful and a violation of this chapter for a person to copy, produce or otherwise bring into existence a facsimile or counterfeit parking permit or permits without written authorization from the Director of Public Works. It shall further be unlawful and a violation of this chapter for a person to knowingly use or display a facsimile or counterfeit parking permit in order to evade limitations on parking applicable in a permit parking zone.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EAny person who violates any of the provisions of this chapter shall be guilty of an infraction, and upon conviction thereof, be punished as provided in Chapter 1.12.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1197, (part), 1982)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"8ac2cb19-fd5f-48fa-907e-3dabb70d879d","prev_id":null}]}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/c0ea64e8-6e08-433b-b7d5-210ed238ccf5","ref":{"parent":"ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":1,"tag":"h3"},"pos":"212-211","docId":"75","text":"CHAPTER 11.28: MISCELLANEOUS PARKING REGULATIONS--ON-STREET PARKING","id":"c0ea64e8-6e08-433b-b7d5-210ed238ccf5","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/c0ea64e8-6e08-433b-b7d5-210ed238ccf5\/4ba97a80-9415-4ddf-b0ed-f6f40c1c63db","ref":{"parent":"c0ea64e8-6e08-433b-b7d5-210ed238ccf5","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-211-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"4ba97a80-9415-4ddf-b0ed-f6f40c1c63db","prev_id":null},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/c0ea64e8-6e08-433b-b7d5-210ed238ccf5\/0d33b501-9a8d-4f68-a0ad-b7a369a50893","ref":{"parent":"c0ea64e8-6e08-433b-b7d5-210ed238ccf5","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-211-12","docId":"75","text":"11.28.010 Definitions.","id":"0d33b501-9a8d-4f68-a0ad-b7a369a50893","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/c0ea64e8-6e08-433b-b7d5-210ed238ccf5\/0d33b501-9a8d-4f68-a0ad-b7a369a50893\/89fa023a-5d64-4d2f-a057-dd7ca678eb22","ref":{"parent":"0d33b501-9a8d-4f68-a0ad-b7a369a50893","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-211-12-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EThe following words and phrases when used in this chapter shall have the meanings set forth in this section:\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Col class=\u0022default-style\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:upper-alpha\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u201cCamp car\u201d means a vehicle with or without motive power which is designed for human habitation and which contains plumbing, heating or electrical equipment.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u201cCommercial vehicle\u201d means any vehicle or part thereof required to be registered under the State of California Vehicle Code, which is used or maintained for the transportation of persons for hire, compensation, or profit, or designed, used or maintained primarily for the transportation of property, except passenger vehicles and house cars.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u201cMobile home\u201d means a vehicle, other than a motor vehicle, designed or used as semipermanent housing, designed for human habitation, for carrying persons and property on its own structure and for being drawn by a motor vehicle, and shall include a trailer coach.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u201cOversized vehicle\u201d shall mean any camp trailer, camper, fifth wheel travel trailer, house car, mobile home, trailer coach, or recreational vehicle as defined in California Vehicle Code Sections 242, 243, 324, 362, 396, 635 and California Health and Safety Code Section 18010. Additionally, any motorized vehicle, or combination of motorized and\/or non-motorized vehicle(s), as defined in California Vehicle Code Section 670, in excess of 22 feet in length, and\/or 6 feet in width and 7 feet in height, will also be considered an \u201coversized vehicle\u201d for purposes of this chapter.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u201cPark\u201d means to stand or leave standing any vehicle, whether occupied or not, otherwise than temporarily for the purpose of and while actually engaged in the loading or unloading of passengers or materials.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u201cPublic streets\u201d means all streets, lanes, places, avenues and portions thereof, including extensions in length and width, which have been dedicated by the owners thereof to public use, acquired for public use, or in which a public easement exists.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u201cStationary mobile equipment\u201d means any equipment, including vehicle(s), used in activities with or without involvement from members of the public, which are not actively moving during use.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u201cTruck trailer\u201d means a commercial vehicle without motive power designed to be drawn by a truck.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u201cVehicle\u201d means any boat, bus, trailer, motor home, van, camper (whether or not attached to a pickup or other vehicle), camp trailer, mobile home, motorcycle, automobile, truck, pickup, airplane, haul trailer, truck tractor, truck trailer, utility trailer, or parts thereof, or any device by which any person or property may be propelled, moved or drawn upon a public street, excepting a device moved exclusively by human power.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1346, (part), 1986; Ord. 276, \u00a7 1, 1964; Ord. 25-2275, \u00a7 1, 2025; Ord. 26-2284, Att. A (part), 2026)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"89fa023a-5d64-4d2f-a057-dd7ca678eb22","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/c0ea64e8-6e08-433b-b7d5-210ed238ccf5\/a625c755-56fe-45d5-bf49-e0e515bae42d","ref":{"parent":"c0ea64e8-6e08-433b-b7d5-210ed238ccf5","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-211-13","docId":"75","text":"11.28.020 Vehicle Parking Regulations.","id":"a625c755-56fe-45d5-bf49-e0e515bae42d","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/c0ea64e8-6e08-433b-b7d5-210ed238ccf5\/a625c755-56fe-45d5-bf49-e0e515bae42d\/5f1c53d8-e45f-498c-8dad-df9fa019c410","ref":{"parent":"a625c755-56fe-45d5-bf49-e0e515bae42d","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-211-13-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Col class=\u0022default-style\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:upper-alpha\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003ELiving or Sleeping Quarters. No vehicle, as defined in this chapter, shall be used for living or sleeping quarters on any public right of way, street, highway, alley, parking lot, park or other state-, county-, or city-owned property.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003ERental of Vehicles for Living or Sleeping Quarters. No person shall rent, lease, let out, or otherwise loan any vehicle, as defined in this chapter, for use as sleeping or living quarters on any public right of way, street, highway, alley, parking lot, park or other state-, county-, or city-owned property in exchange for money, goods, or services.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EMobile Homes. Mobile homes, excluding travel trailers, are not permitted to be parked on public streets within the residential zones of the City.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EUnmounted Campers. It shall be unlawful for any person to place, keep or maintain, or permit to be placed, kept or maintained, any unmounted camper on any public street.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EOversized Vehicle Parking. No person shall stop, stand, park or leave standing any oversized vehicle as defined in this chapter on any public right of way, street, highway, alley, parking lot, park or other state-, county- or city-owned property between the hours of 10 P.M. to 6 A.M. The provisions of this chapter shall not apply to oversized vehicles that have obtained a permit as provided in Chapter 11.27, or that are engaged in commercial activity within the City. Oversized vehicles parked overnight in violation of this chapter shall be guilty of an infraction, and upon conviction thereof, be punished as provided in Chapter 1.12.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003ELoading and Unloading and Utility Vehicles. The provisions of this chapter shall not apply to active loading or unloading of any vehicle, or to any public service or utility company vehicle while in the performance of service or maintenance work.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EConstruction Trailers. Trailers may be used for temporary offices on construction projects. A permit must be obtained from the City Building Department after satisfactory information has been given that the use is in compliance with the conditions of this chapter.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1346, (part), 1986; Ord. 547, \u00a7 1, 1972; Ord. 276, \u00a7 2, 1964; Ord. 25-2275, \u00a7 1, 2025)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"5f1c53d8-e45f-498c-8dad-df9fa019c410","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/c0ea64e8-6e08-433b-b7d5-210ed238ccf5\/13711145-be04-474e-8b5c-8b0d1d3d08b7","ref":{"parent":"c0ea64e8-6e08-433b-b7d5-210ed238ccf5","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-211-14","docId":"75","text":"11.28.030 Commercial Vehicles.","id":"13711145-be04-474e-8b5c-8b0d1d3d08b7","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/c0ea64e8-6e08-433b-b7d5-210ed238ccf5\/13711145-be04-474e-8b5c-8b0d1d3d08b7\/31c687df-b0a1-4600-9118-30bd07b95e56","ref":{"parent":"13711145-be04-474e-8b5c-8b0d1d3d08b7","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-211-14-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Col class=\u0022default-style\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:upper-alpha\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003ECommercial vehicles having a manufacturer\u2019s gross vehicle weight rating of ten thousand pounds or more shall not park or stand on any street located within a residential zoning district.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003ETruck trailers shall not park or stand upon any public street.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1346, (part), 1986; Ord. 276, \u00a7 3, 1964)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"31c687df-b0a1-4600-9118-30bd07b95e56","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/c0ea64e8-6e08-433b-b7d5-210ed238ccf5\/1b7bc91b-cfdf-4487-b6a9-2327eba2b1f4","ref":{"parent":"c0ea64e8-6e08-433b-b7d5-210ed238ccf5","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-211-15","docId":"75","text":"11.28.040 Constructing, Repairing, or Greasing Vehicles on Public Streets.","id":"1b7bc91b-cfdf-4487-b6a9-2327eba2b1f4","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/c0ea64e8-6e08-433b-b7d5-210ed238ccf5\/1b7bc91b-cfdf-4487-b6a9-2327eba2b1f4\/4d2175eb-9559-497c-9c52-e913d21e2607","ref":{"parent":"1b7bc91b-cfdf-4487-b6a9-2327eba2b1f4","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-211-15-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003ENo person shall construct or cause to be constructed, repair or cause to be repaired, grease or cause to be greased, any vehicle or any part thereof upon any public street in the city. Temporary emergency repairs may be made upon a public street.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 276, \u00a7 4, 1964)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"4d2175eb-9559-497c-9c52-e913d21e2607","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/c0ea64e8-6e08-433b-b7d5-210ed238ccf5\/07e06007-f4b5-4151-acfa-75cec5f33ede","ref":{"parent":"c0ea64e8-6e08-433b-b7d5-210ed238ccf5","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-211-16","docId":"75","text":"11.28.050 Sale of Merchandise.","id":"07e06007-f4b5-4151-acfa-75cec5f33ede","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/c0ea64e8-6e08-433b-b7d5-210ed238ccf5\/07e06007-f4b5-4151-acfa-75cec5f33ede\/686f4266-6f1c-4353-9e4f-daa3fca42ae2","ref":{"parent":"07e06007-f4b5-4151-acfa-75cec5f33ede","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-211-16-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EIt is unlawful for any person or persons to sell merchandise, fruits, or vegetables from any stationary mobile equipment on any public street within the city.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 276, \u00a7 5, 1964; Ord. 26-2284, Att. A (part), 2026)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"686f4266-6f1c-4353-9e4f-daa3fca42ae2","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/c0ea64e8-6e08-433b-b7d5-210ed238ccf5\/d8116da5-3472-4511-a390-446afb06ce5a","ref":{"parent":"c0ea64e8-6e08-433b-b7d5-210ed238ccf5","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-211-17","docId":"75","text":"11.28.060 Violation\u2013Penalty.","id":"d8116da5-3472-4511-a390-446afb06ce5a","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/c0ea64e8-6e08-433b-b7d5-210ed238ccf5\/d8116da5-3472-4511-a390-446afb06ce5a\/78f2c3cb-6f21-4ca0-b31a-8ab4c94f4780","ref":{"parent":"d8116da5-3472-4511-a390-446afb06ce5a","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-211-17-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EAny person who violates the provisions of this chapter shall be guilty of an infraction and upon conviction thereof shall be punished as provided in Chapter 1.12.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1179, \u00a7 2 (part), 1982; Ord. 276, \u00a7 7, 1964)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"78f2c3cb-6f21-4ca0-b31a-8ab4c94f4780","prev_id":null}]}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7bf5e89d-f4b6-4c4c-b477-7e8ce0e6d34f","ref":{"parent":"ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":1,"tag":"h3"},"pos":"212-212","docId":"75","text":"CHAPTER 11.30: REGULATION OF TRAFFIC IN THE DOWNTOWN AREA","id":"7bf5e89d-f4b6-4c4c-b477-7e8ce0e6d34f","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7bf5e89d-f4b6-4c4c-b477-7e8ce0e6d34f\/637071c4-a533-4441-b541-f55907770ccf","ref":{"parent":"7bf5e89d-f4b6-4c4c-b477-7e8ce0e6d34f","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-212-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"637071c4-a533-4441-b541-f55907770ccf","prev_id":null},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7bf5e89d-f4b6-4c4c-b477-7e8ce0e6d34f\/0d69df20-6f37-42e6-a6d3-214f8ffe0d6f","ref":{"parent":"7bf5e89d-f4b6-4c4c-b477-7e8ce0e6d34f","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-212-12","docId":"75","text":"11.30.010 Definitions.","id":"0d69df20-6f37-42e6-a6d3-214f8ffe0d6f","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7bf5e89d-f4b6-4c4c-b477-7e8ce0e6d34f\/0d69df20-6f37-42e6-a6d3-214f8ffe0d6f\/7a0d4aa5-7593-4bba-b6d0-3b2cfc254b33","ref":{"parent":"0d69df20-6f37-42e6-a6d3-214f8ffe0d6f","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-212-12-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EThe following definitions apply to this chapter:\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Col class=\u0022default-style\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:upper-alpha\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u201cCentral business district\u201d means Stevens Creek Boulevard bounded by Tantau Avenue to the east and Peninsula Avenue\/Bubb Road to the west; Wolfe Road bounded by Calle De Barcelona to the south and Homestead Road to the north; and De Anza Boulevard bounded by Bollinger Road to the south and Homestead Road to the north.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u201cCruising\u201d is driving a motor vehicle on a highway past a traffic control point designated by a peace officer, under conditions in which traffic is congested at or near the control point, three or more times within a two-hour period, after having driven past said control point twice within the same period and having been given adequate written notice after the second passing that passing the control point a third time under the conditions stated herein shall constitute a violation of this section.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u201cHighway\u201d and \u201cmotor vehicle\u201d are defined in Sections 360 and 415 respectively, of the Vehicle Code.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1211, \u00a7 1 (part), 1982; Ord. 1010, \u00a7 1 (part), 1980)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"7a0d4aa5-7593-4bba-b6d0-3b2cfc254b33","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7bf5e89d-f4b6-4c4c-b477-7e8ce0e6d34f\/69938f61-2a38-401a-b214-5e732b8a6e0d","ref":{"parent":"7bf5e89d-f4b6-4c4c-b477-7e8ce0e6d34f","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-212-13","docId":"75","text":"11.30.020 Exclusions.","id":"69938f61-2a38-401a-b214-5e732b8a6e0d","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7bf5e89d-f4b6-4c4c-b477-7e8ce0e6d34f\/69938f61-2a38-401a-b214-5e732b8a6e0d\/4d9aa365-e084-4971-9102-1b3e52771d18","ref":{"parent":"69938f61-2a38-401a-b214-5e732b8a6e0d","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-212-13-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EThis chapter shall not apply to the following vehicles: emergency vehicles on patrol, taxicabs for hire, and other business vehicles being driven for business purposes.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1211, \u00a7 1 (part), 1982; Ord. 1010, \u00a7 1 (part), 1980)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"4d9aa365-e084-4971-9102-1b3e52771d18","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7bf5e89d-f4b6-4c4c-b477-7e8ce0e6d34f\/8c48ce5e-c774-4932-9be4-0eb73a0bca42","ref":{"parent":"7bf5e89d-f4b6-4c4c-b477-7e8ce0e6d34f","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-212-14","docId":"75","text":"11.30.030 Prohibitions.","id":"8c48ce5e-c774-4932-9be4-0eb73a0bca42","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/7bf5e89d-f4b6-4c4c-b477-7e8ce0e6d34f\/8c48ce5e-c774-4932-9be4-0eb73a0bca42\/40d687cf-e28e-4f85-9c1b-8ca9e5bac8dd","ref":{"parent":"8c48ce5e-c774-4932-9be4-0eb73a0bca42","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-212-14-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003ECruising is prohibited in the \u201ccentral business district.\u201d\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1211, \u00a7 1 (part), 1982; Ord. 1010, \u00a7 1 (part), 1980)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E11.30.040 Violation\u2013Penalty.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EAny person who violates any of the provisions of this chapter shall be guilty of an infraction and upon conviction thereof shall be punished as provided in Chapter 1.12.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1211, \u00a7 1 (part), 1982)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"40d687cf-e28e-4f85-9c1b-8ca9e5bac8dd","prev_id":null}]}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a2d597bb-5c1d-4566-b9d4-6673e20500a5","ref":{"parent":"ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":1,"tag":"h3"},"pos":"212-213","docId":"75","text":"CHAPTER 11.31: REGULATION OF PARKING ON PROPERTY OWNED BY CITY","id":"a2d597bb-5c1d-4566-b9d4-6673e20500a5","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a2d597bb-5c1d-4566-b9d4-6673e20500a5\/c5994160-6bab-4d73-8fd1-7f223df7fe00","ref":{"parent":"a2d597bb-5c1d-4566-b9d4-6673e20500a5","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-213-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"c5994160-6bab-4d73-8fd1-7f223df7fe00","prev_id":null},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a2d597bb-5c1d-4566-b9d4-6673e20500a5\/75e5a0ef-8000-4dd5-a41a-945a4d55a904","ref":{"parent":"a2d597bb-5c1d-4566-b9d4-6673e20500a5","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-213-12","docId":"75","text":"11.31.010 Definitions.","id":"75e5a0ef-8000-4dd5-a41a-945a4d55a904","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a2d597bb-5c1d-4566-b9d4-6673e20500a5\/75e5a0ef-8000-4dd5-a41a-945a4d55a904\/28496560-13ae-4df1-8e3f-f07a6de39204","ref":{"parent":"75e5a0ef-8000-4dd5-a41a-945a4d55a904","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-213-12-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EFor the purpose of this chapter, the following definition applies: \u201cParking\u201d means standing or leaving standing any vehicle, whether occupied or not, otherwise than temporarily for the purpose of and while actually engaged in loading or unloading of passengers or vehicles.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1055, \u00a7 1 (part), 1980)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"28496560-13ae-4df1-8e3f-f07a6de39204","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a2d597bb-5c1d-4566-b9d4-6673e20500a5\/0b21b612-5a42-4676-9e4c-e83252f7fb80","ref":{"parent":"a2d597bb-5c1d-4566-b9d4-6673e20500a5","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-213-13","docId":"75","text":"11.31.020 Prohibition\u2013Limitation\u2013Limitation of Parking.","id":"0b21b612-5a42-4676-9e4c-e83252f7fb80","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a2d597bb-5c1d-4566-b9d4-6673e20500a5\/0b21b612-5a42-4676-9e4c-e83252f7fb80\/2322bb9c-f45b-449e-b188-17ae7ae4e8a7","ref":{"parent":"0b21b612-5a42-4676-9e4c-e83252f7fb80","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-213-13-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Col class=\u0022default-style\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:upper-alpha\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003EWhenever the City Manager determines that the orderly, efficient conduct of the City\u2019s business requires parking or standing of vehicles on City property to be prohibited, limited, or restricted, the City Manager shall have the power and authority to order signs to be erected or posted or markings installed indicating that the parking of vehicles is thus prohibited, limited, or restricted.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003ESuch power and authority shall include ordering signs to be erected or posted designating stalls or spaces for physically handicapped persons in accordance with the provisions of Section 22507.8 of the Vehicle Code of the state of California as the same exists or is hereafter amended, on all off-street parking facilities owned or operated by the City.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1101, 1981; Ord. 1055, \u00a7 1 (part), 1980)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"2322bb9c-f45b-449e-b188-17ae7ae4e8a7","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a2d597bb-5c1d-4566-b9d4-6673e20500a5\/4450c6e3-7561-4a62-b886-b852783c350a","ref":{"parent":"a2d597bb-5c1d-4566-b9d4-6673e20500a5","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-213-14","docId":"75","text":"11.31.030 Unlawful.","id":"4450c6e3-7561-4a62-b886-b852783c350a","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a2d597bb-5c1d-4566-b9d4-6673e20500a5\/4450c6e3-7561-4a62-b886-b852783c350a\/4028ea1e-6800-4a4e-8d0f-80cc69050e94","ref":{"parent":"4450c6e3-7561-4a62-b886-b852783c350a","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-213-14-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EWhenever signs have been erected in a designated area, pursuant to Section 11.31.020, it is unlawful for any person to park or stand any vehicle in said area in violation of the prohibitions, limitations, or restrictions indicated by such signs.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1055, \u00a7 1 (part), 1980)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"4028ea1e-6800-4a4e-8d0f-80cc69050e94","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a2d597bb-5c1d-4566-b9d4-6673e20500a5\/5f517140-089f-4c66-8fa1-b3aef8d261d9","ref":{"parent":"a2d597bb-5c1d-4566-b9d4-6673e20500a5","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-213-15","docId":"75","text":"11.31.040 Violation\u2013Penalty.","id":"5f517140-089f-4c66-8fa1-b3aef8d261d9","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a2d597bb-5c1d-4566-b9d4-6673e20500a5\/5f517140-089f-4c66-8fa1-b3aef8d261d9\/1bdb9bef-5cad-4529-9896-7d5cd1b1ff35","ref":{"parent":"5f517140-089f-4c66-8fa1-b3aef8d261d9","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-213-15-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EAny person who violates any of the provisions of this chapter shall be guilty of an infraction and upon conviction thereof shall be punished as provided in Chapter 1.12 of this code.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1055, \u00a7 1 (part), 1980)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"1bdb9bef-5cad-4529-9896-7d5cd1b1ff35","prev_id":null}]}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a498924b-6528-4cf3-ba6d-3dc7c22f9065","ref":{"parent":"ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":1,"tag":"h3"},"pos":"212-214","docId":"75","text":"CHAPTER 11.32: TRUCK TRAFFIC ROUTES","id":"a498924b-6528-4cf3-ba6d-3dc7c22f9065","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a498924b-6528-4cf3-ba6d-3dc7c22f9065\/125cc54e-db11-4edd-ba65-264e97d8c1e5","ref":{"parent":"a498924b-6528-4cf3-ba6d-3dc7c22f9065","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-214-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"125cc54e-db11-4edd-ba65-264e97d8c1e5","prev_id":null},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a498924b-6528-4cf3-ba6d-3dc7c22f9065\/226aaa28-2135-4fee-84d3-2defcab55083","ref":{"parent":"a498924b-6528-4cf3-ba6d-3dc7c22f9065","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-214-12","docId":"75","text":"11.32.010 Definitions.","id":"226aaa28-2135-4fee-84d3-2defcab55083","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a498924b-6528-4cf3-ba6d-3dc7c22f9065\/226aaa28-2135-4fee-84d3-2defcab55083\/c45a0023-e828-4e0d-9285-ef4f0022613f","ref":{"parent":"226aaa28-2135-4fee-84d3-2defcab55083","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-214-12-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EFor purposes of this chapter:\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Col class=\u0022default-style\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:upper-alpha\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe term \u201ctruck\u201d means any vehicle as defined in the Vehicle Code of California, or as hereafter amended, that exceeds a gross weight of three tons and has a total combination of motor truck, truck tractor and\/or trailers of sixty feet or less in length.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe phrase \u201cinterstate truck\u201d means any vehicle as defined in the Vehicle Code of California, or as hereafter amended, that exceeds a maximum gross weight of three tons and has a total combination of motor truck, truck tractor and\/or trailers that exceeds sixty feet in length.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe term \u201cpublic school\u201d means an elementary or secondary school supported by public funds and providing free education for children in grades K - 12.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 15-2128, \u00a7 2, 2015; Ord. 1267, \u00a7 1 (part), 1984; Ord. 833, \u00a7 2, 1977)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"c45a0023-e828-4e0d-9285-ef4f0022613f","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a498924b-6528-4cf3-ba6d-3dc7c22f9065\/9f540cd6-c66f-4076-ab2c-8d179f4c6739","ref":{"parent":"a498924b-6528-4cf3-ba6d-3dc7c22f9065","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-214-13","docId":"75","text":"11.32.020 Routes\u2013Established\u2013Signs.","id":"9f540cd6-c66f-4076-ab2c-8d179f4c6739","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a498924b-6528-4cf3-ba6d-3dc7c22f9065\/9f540cd6-c66f-4076-ab2c-8d179f4c6739\/e84706e0-1f0d-4084-adde-3afa925f3b9f","ref":{"parent":"9f540cd6-c66f-4076-ab2c-8d179f4c6739","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-214-13-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EA. The following truck traffic routes within the City are hereby established for the movement of any truck as defined in Section 11.32.010:\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Ctable cellpadding=\u00220\u0022 cellspacing=\u00220\u0022 style=\u0022width:600px\u0022\u003E\u003Cthead\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Cth scope=\u0022col\u0022 style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EStreet\u003C\/strong\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/th\u003E\u003Cth scope=\u0022col\u0022 style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003ELimits\u003C\/strong\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/th\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003C\/thead\u003E\u003Ctbody\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EDe Anza Boulevard\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EFrom the South City Limits to the North City Limits, all portions currently or hereafter within the City Limits.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EFoothill Boulevard\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EFrom McClellan Road to Junipero Serra Freeway (Route No. 280), all portions currently or hereafter within the City Limits.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EHomestead Road\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EFrom Stevens Creek Freeway (Route 85) to Lawrence Expressway, all portions currently or hereafter within the City Limits.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EStevens Canyon Road\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EFrom the South City Limits to McClellan Road, all portions currently or hereafter within the City Limits.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EStevens Creek Boulevard\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EFrom the West City Limits to Foothill Boulevard and from West Valley Freeway (Route No. 85) to the East City Limits, all portions currently or hereafter within the city limits.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003ETantau Avenue\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EFrom Stevens Creek Boulevard to Homestead Road.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EWolfe Road\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EStevens Creek Boulevard to Homestead Road.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003C\/tbody\u003E\u003C\/table\u003E\u003Cp\u003EB. The City Engineer is directed to designate the above-named truck traffic routes by the erection of appropriate approved state standard signs giving notice to the ordinance codified in this chapter.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 15-2134, \u00a7 1, 2015; Ord. 833, \u00a7 3, 1977)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"e84706e0-1f0d-4084-adde-3afa925f3b9f","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a498924b-6528-4cf3-ba6d-3dc7c22f9065\/31a0996d-235a-4f55-8936-fe4cfb0a9e27","ref":{"parent":"a498924b-6528-4cf3-ba6d-3dc7c22f9065","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-214-14","docId":"75","text":"11.32.030 Routes\u2013Signs\u2013Compliance.","id":"31a0996d-235a-4f55-8936-fe4cfb0a9e27","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a498924b-6528-4cf3-ba6d-3dc7c22f9065\/31a0996d-235a-4f55-8936-fe4cfb0a9e27\/d8139264-99e1-4bca-9729-16ae0ef80f6c","ref":{"parent":"31a0996d-235a-4f55-8936-fe4cfb0a9e27","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-214-14-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EWhen authorized signs are in place giving notice of designated traffic truck routes, no person shall operate, drive, or cause or permit to be operated or driven a truck as defined in Section 11.32.010 of this chapter on any street or streets within the City other than on a truck traffic route, except as otherwise provided in this chapter.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 833, \u00a7 4, 1977)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"d8139264-99e1-4bca-9729-16ae0ef80f6c","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a498924b-6528-4cf3-ba6d-3dc7c22f9065\/ebfb1fb3-9548-4a1e-b61d-0e045190c7da","ref":{"parent":"a498924b-6528-4cf3-ba6d-3dc7c22f9065","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-214-15","docId":"75","text":"11.32.040 Authority to Require Weighing of Vehicle.","id":"ebfb1fb3-9548-4a1e-b61d-0e045190c7da","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a498924b-6528-4cf3-ba6d-3dc7c22f9065\/ebfb1fb3-9548-4a1e-b61d-0e045190c7da\/869cf028-2cb3-4560-952a-3255086ab1ff","ref":{"parent":"ebfb1fb3-9548-4a1e-b61d-0e045190c7da","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-214-15-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EAny peace officer having jurisdiction within the City, or acting under its authority, shall have the authority to require any person driving or in control of any vehicle as defined in the Vehicle Code of California, or as hereafter amended, not proceeding over a truck traffic route to proceed to any public or private scale available for the purpose of weighing and determining whether this chapter has been complied with.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 833, \u00a7 5, 1977)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"869cf028-2cb3-4560-952a-3255086ab1ff","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a498924b-6528-4cf3-ba6d-3dc7c22f9065\/700f6b1b-ca71-4704-af25-bbe9e5681766","ref":{"parent":"a498924b-6528-4cf3-ba6d-3dc7c22f9065","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-214-16","docId":"75","text":"11.32.050 Unrestricted Highways\u2013Interstate Trucks.","id":"700f6b1b-ca71-4704-af25-bbe9e5681766","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a498924b-6528-4cf3-ba6d-3dc7c22f9065\/700f6b1b-ca71-4704-af25-bbe9e5681766\/0e3925eb-9d3c-4c29-9b0a-dc91fe2f48c1","ref":{"parent":"700f6b1b-ca71-4704-af25-bbe9e5681766","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-214-16-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003ENothing contained in this chapter is intended to regulate the movement of any vehicle as defined in the Vehicle Code of California, or as hereafter amended, upon any of the following named highways, portions of which are located within the City, and which are referred to in this chapter as \u201cunrestricted highways\u201d:\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Ctable cellpadding=\u00220\u0022 cellspacing=\u00220\u0022 style=\u0022width:600px\u0022\u003E\u003Ctbody\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EDe Anza Boulevard (Route # 85)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EFoothill Expressway\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EJunipero Serra Freeway (Route # 280)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003Ctr\u003E\u003Ctd style=\u0022vertical-align:top\u0022\u003E\u003Cp\u003EWest Valley Freeway (Route # 85)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003C\/td\u003E\u003C\/tr\u003E\u003C\/tbody\u003E\u003C\/table\u003E\u003Cp\u003EUnless otherwise permitted in this chapter, no person shall operate, drive or cause or permit to be operated or driven, an interstate truck as defined in Section 11.32.010 of this chapter on any street or streets within the City other than on unrestricted highways.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1267, \u00a7 1 (part), 1984; Ord. 833, \u00a7 6, 1977)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"0e3925eb-9d3c-4c29-9b0a-dc91fe2f48c1","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a498924b-6528-4cf3-ba6d-3dc7c22f9065\/f7388ed5-9994-4eda-ba16-c1e7136877f6","ref":{"parent":"a498924b-6528-4cf3-ba6d-3dc7c22f9065","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-214-17","docId":"75","text":"11.32.055 School Zones\u2014Prohibited vehicles.","id":"f7388ed5-9994-4eda-ba16-c1e7136877f6","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a498924b-6528-4cf3-ba6d-3dc7c22f9065\/f7388ed5-9994-4eda-ba16-c1e7136877f6\/615a91cc-31f8-4387-8e9c-4a49fd3d20c9","ref":{"parent":"f7388ed5-9994-4eda-ba16-c1e7136877f6","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-214-17-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Col class=\u0022default-style\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:upper-alpha\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003ENo person shall operate, drive, or cause or permit to be operated or driven, any truck, as defined in Section 11.32.010 of this chapter, between the hours of 7:00 a.m. and 9:30 a.m. in the morning and the hours of 2:00 p.m. and 4:00 p.m. in the afternoon Monday through Friday, on the following roadway segments:\u003Col class=\u0022paren-value-paren\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:lower-roman\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003Eon any roadway which runs contiguous to and is within 500 feet of any public school grounds;\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EMcClellan Road, between Stelling Road and Bubb Road.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe only vehicles which can operate during the times listed in Section 11.32.055(a) are as follows:\u003Col class=\u0022paren-value-paren\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:lower-roman\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003EEmergency response vehicles;\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EAny vehicle traveling on an arterial or major collector avenues as defined in the City of Cupertino\u2019s General Plan, Chapter 5, \u201cMobility Element\u201d, Figure M-2, including DeAnza Boulevard, Homestead Road, Stevens Creek Boulevard (east of Foothill Boulevard), Wolfe Road (north of Stevens Creek), Bollinger Road (east of DeAnza Boulevard), Bubb Road (north of McClellan Road), Foothill Boulevard (north of Stevens creek), Miller Avenue (north of Bollinger Road), Stelling Road (north of Stevens Creek) and Tantau (north of Stevens Creek Boulevard).\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003ESolid waste, garbage, or recycling trucks and street sweepers operating on their established routes;\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EA public utility or licensed contractor while necessarily in use in the construction, installation, or in repair of any public utility, within the City, but only as necessary for emergency repair; or\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EPassenger buses and other public transit vehicles under the jurisdiction of the California Public Utilities Commission, school buses, and employer- sponsored passenger buses provided solely fo the employer\u2019s employees, so long as these vehicles do not deviate from their established route(s).\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe Director of Public Works is directed to designate the above-named school zones by the erection of appropriate approved state standard signs giving notice of the restrictions in this section.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EWhen authorized signs are in place giving notice of the designated school zones, no person shall operate, drive, or cause or permit a truck to be operated or driven in violation of this section unless otherwise exempt under the provisions of subsection B of this section.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 15-2134, \u00a7 2, 2015; Ord. 15-2128, \u00a7 3, 2015)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"615a91cc-31f8-4387-8e9c-4a49fd3d20c9","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a498924b-6528-4cf3-ba6d-3dc7c22f9065\/98fe4252-bad7-4104-b861-acaeb1d3312e","ref":{"parent":"a498924b-6528-4cf3-ba6d-3dc7c22f9065","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-214-18","docId":"75","text":"11.32.060 Truck Traffic\u2013Origin and Destination Points.","id":"98fe4252-bad7-4104-b861-acaeb1d3312e","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a498924b-6528-4cf3-ba6d-3dc7c22f9065\/98fe4252-bad7-4104-b861-acaeb1d3312e\/eb0a73bd-7115-41f8-ac74-81777ec658d1","ref":{"parent":"98fe4252-bad7-4104-b861-acaeb1d3312e","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-214-18-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Col class=\u0022default-style\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:upper-alpha\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003EAny truck as defined in Section 11.32.010 of this chapter entering the City for a destination point outside the City shall proceed only over a truck traffic route or other unrestricted highway.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EAny truck as defined in Section 11.32.010 of this chapter on a trip originating within the City and traveling in the City for a destination point outside of the City shall proceed by the shortest and most direct route to the nearest truck traffic route or other unrestricted highway.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EAny truck as defined in Section 11.32.010 of this chapter entering the City for one or more destination points in the City shall proceed only over a truck traffic route or other unrestricted highway, and shall deviate therefrom only by the shortest and most direct route between each destination point and the nearest truck traffic route or other unrestricted highway.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EAny truck as defined in Section 11.32.010 of this chapter on a trip originating in the City, and traveling in the City for one or more destination points in the City, shall proceed by the shortest and most direct route to the nearest truck traffic route or other unrestricted highway, and shall deviate therefrom only by the shortest and most direct route between each destination point and the nearest truck traffic route or other unrestricted highway.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EAny truck as defined in Section 11.32.010 of this chapter traveling in the City for more than one destination point in the City may proceed directly from one destination point to the next destination point by the shortest and most direct route without returning to the nearest truck traffic route or other unrestricted highway, if it will result in a shorter distance being traveled on streets upon which such a truck ordinarily would not be allowed to travel notwithstanding the requirements of subsections C and D of this section.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 833, \u00a7 7, 1977)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"eb0a73bd-7115-41f8-ac74-81777ec658d1","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a498924b-6528-4cf3-ba6d-3dc7c22f9065\/f6aecb38-8db0-4c0c-8391-59884e8dea20","ref":{"parent":"a498924b-6528-4cf3-ba6d-3dc7c22f9065","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-214-19","docId":"75","text":"11.32.070 Exceptions\u2013Pickup or Delivery.","id":"f6aecb38-8db0-4c0c-8391-59884e8dea20","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a498924b-6528-4cf3-ba6d-3dc7c22f9065\/f6aecb38-8db0-4c0c-8391-59884e8dea20\/d19f8e8e-ef65-49a2-91df-6aea0b1c188a","ref":{"parent":"f6aecb38-8db0-4c0c-8391-59884e8dea20","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-214-19-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EFor the purpose of this chapter, a \u201crestricted street\u201d is any street which is neither a truck traffic route nor an unrestricted highway. This section does not apply to the time restrictions around school zones as set forth in Section 11.32.055. Except during the times as set forth in Section 11.32.055, nothing contained in this chapter shall prohibit the operation of any commercial vehicle as defined in the Vehicle Code of California, or as hereafter amended, coming from a truck traffic route or unrestricted highway having ingress or egress by direct route to and from a restricted street when necessary for the purpose of making pickups or deliveries of goods, wares and merchandise from or to any building or structure located on the restricted street, or for the purpose of delivering materials to be used in the actual and bona fide repair, alteration, remodeling, or construction of any building or structure upon the restricted street for which a building permit previously has been obtained.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 15-2134, \u00a7 3, 2015; Ord. 833, \u00a7 8, 1977)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"d19f8e8e-ef65-49a2-91df-6aea0b1c188a","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a498924b-6528-4cf3-ba6d-3dc7c22f9065\/7e1b7c5e-4a17-4e55-ad22-50b4d9df6eeb","ref":{"parent":"a498924b-6528-4cf3-ba6d-3dc7c22f9065","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-214-210","docId":"75","text":"11.32.080 Exceptions\u2013Types of Vehicles.","id":"7e1b7c5e-4a17-4e55-ad22-50b4d9df6eeb","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a498924b-6528-4cf3-ba6d-3dc7c22f9065\/7e1b7c5e-4a17-4e55-ad22-50b4d9df6eeb\/39019f66-00d0-454f-8edb-a75f48e9aab8","ref":{"parent":"7e1b7c5e-4a17-4e55-ad22-50b4d9df6eeb","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-214-210-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EExcept as provided in Section 11.32.055, the provisions of this chapter shall not apply to any of the following:\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Col class=\u0022default-style\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:upper-alpha\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003EPassenger buses under the jurisdiction of the Public Utilities Commission of California, and school buses;\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EAny authorized emergency vehicle as defined in Section 165 of the Vehicle Code of California, or as hereafter amended;\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EAny vehicle owned, leased, operated or controlled by:\u003Col class=\u0022paren-value-paren\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:lower-roman\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe City of Cupertino,\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EA contractor retained to provide street sweeping within the City of Cupertino but only while its truck are operating on an established route or traveling to and from an established route,\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EA public utility or licensed contractor while necessarily in use in the construction, installation, or in repair of any public utility, within the City,\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe holder of a franchise issued by the City for the removal of garbage, solid waste, or recycling but only while its trucks are operating on an established route or traveling to and from an established route; and\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EAn employer providing transportation to its employees, provided such vehicles deviate from a truck traffic route or unrestricted highway only by way of a direct route to and from a restricted street and only when necessary for the purpose of picking up or dropping off passengers.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 15-2134, \u00a7 4, 2015; Ord. 833, \u00a7 9, 1977)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"39019f66-00d0-454f-8edb-a75f48e9aab8","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a498924b-6528-4cf3-ba6d-3dc7c22f9065\/609ece39-3097-40e8-9747-caa1be480545","ref":{"parent":"a498924b-6528-4cf3-ba6d-3dc7c22f9065","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-214-211","docId":"75","text":"11.32.090 Violation\u2013Penalty.","id":"609ece39-3097-40e8-9747-caa1be480545","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/a498924b-6528-4cf3-ba6d-3dc7c22f9065\/609ece39-3097-40e8-9747-caa1be480545\/675ce425-f822-4439-b78c-6fa5b45c1c43","ref":{"parent":"609ece39-3097-40e8-9747-caa1be480545","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-214-211-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EAny person, firm, or corporation violating any of the provisions of this chapter shall be deemed guilty of a misdemeanor, and upon conviction thereof shall be punished as provided in Chapter 1.12 of this code.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1731, (part), 1996; Ord. 1196, \u00a7 1, 1982; Ord. 1179, \u00a7 2 (part), 1982; Ord. 833, \u00a7 11, 1977)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"675ce425-f822-4439-b78c-6fa5b45c1c43","prev_id":null}]}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/cbe87632-273d-407a-8fce-85ed66c0de29","ref":{"parent":"ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":1,"tag":"h3"},"pos":"212-215","docId":"75","text":"CHAPTER 11.34: ROADWAY DESIGN FEATURES","id":"cbe87632-273d-407a-8fce-85ed66c0de29","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/cbe87632-273d-407a-8fce-85ed66c0de29\/93430c3d-1099-4c01-9051-0fc7e3569254","ref":{"parent":"cbe87632-273d-407a-8fce-85ed66c0de29","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-215-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"93430c3d-1099-4c01-9051-0fc7e3569254","prev_id":null},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/cbe87632-273d-407a-8fce-85ed66c0de29\/2eaa22f4-d04a-465d-a846-1409be0d2a6d","ref":{"parent":"cbe87632-273d-407a-8fce-85ed66c0de29","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-215-12","docId":"75","text":"11.34.010 Road Bump\u2013Definition.","id":"2eaa22f4-d04a-465d-a846-1409be0d2a6d","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/cbe87632-273d-407a-8fce-85ed66c0de29\/2eaa22f4-d04a-465d-a846-1409be0d2a6d\/859ccc20-8da8-481d-af12-80a621114402","ref":{"parent":"2eaa22f4-d04a-465d-a846-1409be0d2a6d","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-215-12-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EA bump is a vertical rise in the surface of the pavement of three to three and one-quarter inches at its midpoint. The profile is generally parabolic and twelve feet in length. There is no vertical displacement start to finish of the road bump. The shape is consistent for the full width of the pavement except for the last one foot at each end. The ends will be tapered so that they are flush with the roadway at the edge of pavement or at the tip of a gutter.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1837, 1999; Ord. 1430, (part), 1987)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"859ccc20-8da8-481d-af12-80a621114402","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/cbe87632-273d-407a-8fce-85ed66c0de29\/42646ce2-6fb4-458c-8c95-321ab919d055","ref":{"parent":"cbe87632-273d-407a-8fce-85ed66c0de29","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-215-13","docId":"75","text":"11.34.020 Administrative Authority.","id":"42646ce2-6fb4-458c-8c95-321ab919d055","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/cbe87632-273d-407a-8fce-85ed66c0de29\/42646ce2-6fb4-458c-8c95-321ab919d055\/d12e872c-4051-4293-b71b-69b99644470e","ref":{"parent":"42646ce2-6fb4-458c-8c95-321ab919d055","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-215-13-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EThere are conferred upon the City Manager those powers and duties necessary for the administration of this chapter. In addition, there is also conferred upon the City Manager the authority and power to designate such officers and employees of the City, and of other cooperating public agencies, such as the Sheriff\u2019s Department and Fire Department, as may be required to assist him in carrying out the intent and purpose of this chapter.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1838, 1999; Ord. 1430, (part), 1987)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"d12e872c-4051-4293-b71b-69b99644470e","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/cbe87632-273d-407a-8fce-85ed66c0de29\/675e573d-66b6-41c6-a857-3a646d420682","ref":{"parent":"cbe87632-273d-407a-8fce-85ed66c0de29","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-215-14","docId":"75","text":"11.34.030 Warrants for the Installation and Maintenance of Road Bumps.","id":"675e573d-66b6-41c6-a857-3a646d420682","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/cbe87632-273d-407a-8fce-85ed66c0de29\/675e573d-66b6-41c6-a857-3a646d420682\/3942f895-c9ba-443e-b76a-df174909073c","ref":{"parent":"675e573d-66b6-41c6-a857-3a646d420682","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-215-14-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003ERoad bumps may be installed and maintained on streets where all of the following criteria have been and continue to be satisfied.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Col class=\u0022default-style\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:upper-alpha\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe (local or collector) street is a neighborhood residential street as defined by the California Vehicle Code or by City Council actions.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe street is no wider than forty feet from curb to curb or from edge of pavement to edge of pavement.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe street contains no more than one lane in each direction.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EA speed limit of twenty-five miles per hour has been established in conformance with State law.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe street is not a truck route or a transit bus route.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe street has an average annual daily traffic volume of less than four thousand vehicles.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe street has a maximum grade of five percent or less for any segment between intersections.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe minimum distance from an intersection or curve to the road bump shall be one hundred fifty feet.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe spacing between road bumps shall be a minimum of four hundred feet and a maximum of five hundred fifty feet.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe road bump is visible for a distance of one hundred fifty feet.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe result of a traffic and engineering survey must indicate a minimum eighty-five percent approach speed of thirty-two miles per hour.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1847, 2000; Ord. 1839, 1999; Ord. 1430, (part), 1987)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"3942f895-c9ba-443e-b76a-df174909073c","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/cbe87632-273d-407a-8fce-85ed66c0de29\/e456da69-a0bf-4d29-a6d0-3a64e5eaafce","ref":{"parent":"cbe87632-273d-407a-8fce-85ed66c0de29","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-215-15","docId":"75","text":"11.34.040 Road Bump Installation\u2013Authority.","id":"e456da69-a0bf-4d29-a6d0-3a64e5eaafce","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/cbe87632-273d-407a-8fce-85ed66c0de29\/e456da69-a0bf-4d29-a6d0-3a64e5eaafce\/6bb09c46-b60c-414c-b7f2-808704868a01","ref":{"parent":"e456da69-a0bf-4d29-a6d0-3a64e5eaafce","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-215-15-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003ENotwithstanding the criteria provided in Section 11.34.030 of this chapter, the Director of Public Works is authorized to make adjustments in the installation criteria for roadway design features, if, in his professional opinion, such adjustments are necessary for the installation to fit the specific conditions on the residential street where it is installed.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1896, \u00a7 1, 2002)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"6bb09c46-b60c-414c-b7f2-808704868a01","prev_id":null}]}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/8055fbfc-066e-4d1f-bb6f-914525cbd5cb","ref":{"parent":"ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":1,"tag":"h3"},"pos":"212-216","docId":"75","text":"CHAPTER 11.36: CLOSURE OF CURBS AND MEDIANS TO VEHICULAR TRAFFIC","id":"8055fbfc-066e-4d1f-bb6f-914525cbd5cb","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/8055fbfc-066e-4d1f-bb6f-914525cbd5cb\/902ea5af-e6c0-47ca-b857-a05c6cab8130","ref":{"parent":"8055fbfc-066e-4d1f-bb6f-914525cbd5cb","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-216-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"902ea5af-e6c0-47ca-b857-a05c6cab8130","prev_id":null},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/8055fbfc-066e-4d1f-bb6f-914525cbd5cb\/5a9990e0-131c-4cc8-9536-1cd2d1d19181","ref":{"parent":"8055fbfc-066e-4d1f-bb6f-914525cbd5cb","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-216-12","docId":"75","text":"11.36.010 Purpose\u2013Definitions.","id":"5a9990e0-131c-4cc8-9536-1cd2d1d19181","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/8055fbfc-066e-4d1f-bb6f-914525cbd5cb\/5a9990e0-131c-4cc8-9536-1cd2d1d19181\/4f6224e8-fcfe-4927-932a-33d0a856ccf2","ref":{"parent":"5a9990e0-131c-4cc8-9536-1cd2d1d19181","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-216-12-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Col class=\u0022default-style\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:upper-alpha\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003EPursuant to the authority granted by the California Vehicle Code, \u00a7 \u00a7 21100 (d), 21351, 22113, 21651 to regulate and guide vehicular traffic through the use of official traffic-control devices, the City Council of the City of Cupertino finds and declares as follows:\u003Cbr\u003E\n\u003Cbr\u003E\nThe passage of automobile traffic through openings in street curbs and median traffic dividers can and does constitute in some circumstances a hazard to the public safety and an obstacle to the efficient flow of vehicular traffic. Authority is hereby granted therefor, to close such curb openings either temporarily or permanently, in response to public emergencies, road construction, changing or hazardous traffic patterns, and other considerations of public safety and convenience, in accordance with the procedures set forth in this chapter.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EAs used in this chapter:\u003Col\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u201cAffected area\u201d means those particular parcels of real property to which vehicular access customarily and conveniently may be had by use of the curb opening proposed to be closed. Where a private driveway is proposed to be closed, the affected area shall include those properties served by said driveway. Where a median opening is proposed to be closed, the affected area shall include those residences, businesses or other properties within an area reasonably calculated to encompass all of those properties deriving a substantial economic benefit from public use of said opening.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u201cAffected person\u201d means any person or legal entity owning or controlling real property located within the City of Cupertino, who asserts an interest in or valuable right affected by a proposed closure of a curb opening.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u201cCurb opening\u201d means a driveway, curb cut, ramp or aperture in the median or outer border of a street, whereby vehicular travel across such a street border is facilitated. Curb openings as used in this chapter include those giving access from streets to adjacent properties and across medians or center traffic lane dividers.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u201cStreet\u201d means any residential or commercial roadway publicly maintained and open to the use of the public within the City limits of the City of Cupertino which is subject to local regulation as authorized by the California Vehicle Code.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 904, (part), 1978)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"4f6224e8-fcfe-4927-932a-33d0a856ccf2","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/8055fbfc-066e-4d1f-bb6f-914525cbd5cb\/0144fa33-14de-4dad-a229-de63a447a4b5","ref":{"parent":"8055fbfc-066e-4d1f-bb6f-914525cbd5cb","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-216-13","docId":"75","text":"11.36.020 Nonexclusiveness.","id":"0144fa33-14de-4dad-a229-de63a447a4b5","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/8055fbfc-066e-4d1f-bb6f-914525cbd5cb\/0144fa33-14de-4dad-a229-de63a447a4b5\/ba4499c9-820a-4842-b3cf-ecb46fc656b8","ref":{"parent":"0144fa33-14de-4dad-a229-de63a447a4b5","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-216-13-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EThis chapter provides an additional, alternative procedure for the closure of curb openings by the City of Cupertino. It is supplemental to and not exclusive of all other regulatory provisions, statutes or ordinances provided by any public agency having jurisdiction, including the power of officers of the City of Cupertino to respond to a public emergency through proper exercise of inherent police powers.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 904, (part), 1978)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"ba4499c9-820a-4842-b3cf-ecb46fc656b8","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/8055fbfc-066e-4d1f-bb6f-914525cbd5cb\/7de2435a-7566-4b59-b36e-0a080deccfca","ref":{"parent":"8055fbfc-066e-4d1f-bb6f-914525cbd5cb","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-216-14","docId":"75","text":"11.36.030 Closure Authority\u2013General.","id":"7de2435a-7566-4b59-b36e-0a080deccfca","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/8055fbfc-066e-4d1f-bb6f-914525cbd5cb\/7de2435a-7566-4b59-b36e-0a080deccfca\/a99c995e-901b-4292-a0ef-09a749362dbb","ref":{"parent":"7de2435a-7566-4b59-b36e-0a080deccfca","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-216-14-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EIn the event that a public emergency, road construction, hazardous traffic pattern or other considerations make such closure necessary and convenient for reasons of the public safety and welfare the City Manager is empowered to close curb openings in accordance with the procedures stated in this chapter.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 904, (part), 1978)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"a99c995e-901b-4292-a0ef-09a749362dbb","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/8055fbfc-066e-4d1f-bb6f-914525cbd5cb\/8f3844e0-3721-4d7a-a118-c2c07fc158c3","ref":{"parent":"8055fbfc-066e-4d1f-bb6f-914525cbd5cb","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-216-15","docId":"75","text":"11.36.040 Notice of Intention to Close Curb Opening.","id":"8f3844e0-3721-4d7a-a118-c2c07fc158c3","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/8055fbfc-066e-4d1f-bb6f-914525cbd5cb\/8f3844e0-3721-4d7a-a118-c2c07fc158c3\/5a3f8e13-dbd6-448d-9d21-a14735f9b2e5","ref":{"parent":"8f3844e0-3721-4d7a-a118-c2c07fc158c3","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-216-15-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EAt least ten days prior to actual closure of a curb opening a notice of intention to close said curb opening shall be mailed by registered mail to all owners of real property within the affected area, as defined in Section 11.36.010(4), or to the street address of all business or residences within said area or to a combination of said persons and addresses, if the purpose of affording proper notice to affected persons will be served thereby.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe notices of intention shall be in substantially the following form:\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003ENotice of intention to close driveway, median, or other curb opening to vehicular traffic\u003C\/strong\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003ETO: [Name and address of owner or occupant of property within the affected area]\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003ENotice is hereby given pursuant to Chapter 11.36 of the Cupertino Municipal Code that the undersigned has determined that continued vehicular traffic through the driveway median or other curb opening located at\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E[address and other description]\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003Econstitutes a hazard to the public safety and an obstacle to vehicular traffic within the City of Cupertino, in the following particulars:\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cu\u003E[specify] \u003C\/u\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003ENotice is hereby given that the abovedescribed curb opening will be temporarily closed to vehicular traffic beginning on [date] , 19 , by placement of traffic barriers therein.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003ENotice is hereby given that any affected person may address any complaint, comment or protest to:\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EOffice of the City Manager\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003ECity Hall\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E10330 Torre Avenue\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003ECupertino, CA 95014\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Telephone: 252-4505)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003Eat any time following receipt of this notice. Any affected person may request a public hearing regarding this matter, to be held at the next regularly scheduled meeting of the Cupertino City Council. Said public hearing shall be held for the purpose of considering all relevant evidence, and for the purpose of determining whether closure of said curb opening shall be made permanent.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003ENotice mailed on [date] , 19\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\/s\/\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003ECITY MANAGER, City of Cupertino\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 904, (part), 1978)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"5a3f8e13-dbd6-448d-9d21-a14735f9b2e5","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/8055fbfc-066e-4d1f-bb6f-914525cbd5cb\/613b9c59-1a7b-409b-9119-5687ffb2d477","ref":{"parent":"8055fbfc-066e-4d1f-bb6f-914525cbd5cb","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-216-16","docId":"75","text":"11.36.050 Closure Pending Hearing\u2013Authority.","id":"613b9c59-1a7b-409b-9119-5687ffb2d477","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/8055fbfc-066e-4d1f-bb6f-914525cbd5cb\/613b9c59-1a7b-409b-9119-5687ffb2d477\/5d84a888-2806-43ca-9ba3-612bd6dd09ea","ref":{"parent":"613b9c59-1a7b-409b-9119-5687ffb2d477","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-216-16-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EThe City Manager is hereby empowered to close curb openings to vehicular traffic with or without notice if in response to a public emergency, or upon the expiration of ten days following mailing of proper notice as described in Section 11.36.040. Requests for a public hearing shall be addressed to the office of City Manager, who shall forward them to the City Council for action. The City manager may, in his discretion, refrain from closure of any curb opening pending a public hearing on the matter if to do so will serve the public interest.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 904, (part), 1978)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"5d84a888-2806-43ca-9ba3-612bd6dd09ea","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/8055fbfc-066e-4d1f-bb6f-914525cbd5cb\/e6e1909e-10d7-4fd9-97b7-ac25ac25d5e5","ref":{"parent":"8055fbfc-066e-4d1f-bb6f-914525cbd5cb","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-216-17","docId":"75","text":"11.36.060 Hearing\u2013Appeal.","id":"e6e1909e-10d7-4fd9-97b7-ac25ac25d5e5","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/8055fbfc-066e-4d1f-bb6f-914525cbd5cb\/e6e1909e-10d7-4fd9-97b7-ac25ac25d5e5\/c69840ce-1146-4ef0-a45c-987f796b480f","ref":{"parent":"e6e1909e-10d7-4fd9-97b7-ac25ac25d5e5","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-216-17-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Col class=\u0022default-style\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:upper-alpha\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003EUpon receipt of a request for a public hearing, the City Council shall cause such a hearing to be held at its next regular meeting. The City Council may in its discretion convene a special meeting for the purpose of publicly hearing evidence regarding closure of a curb opening.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EAt a public meeting held to review actions taken pursuant to this chapter, the City Council shall hear all evidence and testimony it deems relevant, including the testimony of affected persons. Said hearing may be continued as appropriate, and shall result in a determination whether any curb openings shall be temporarily or permanently closed to vehicular traffic, subject to such other terms and conditions as may be imposed by the City Council. Any determination of the City Council reached as a result of said hearing shall be final, and any rehearing or modification of findings in the matter shall be afforded or not solely within the discretion of the City Council.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 904, (part), 1978)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"c69840ce-1146-4ef0-a45c-987f796b480f","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/8055fbfc-066e-4d1f-bb6f-914525cbd5cb\/40606229-760c-40c6-aa36-0e3fca9864ac","ref":{"parent":"8055fbfc-066e-4d1f-bb6f-914525cbd5cb","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-216-18","docId":"75","text":"11.36.070 Regulation of Traffic During Road Construction.","id":"40606229-760c-40c6-aa36-0e3fca9864ac","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/8055fbfc-066e-4d1f-bb6f-914525cbd5cb\/40606229-760c-40c6-aa36-0e3fca9864ac\/125b8182-864e-45db-a54d-6315f3c629cc","ref":{"parent":"40606229-760c-40c6-aa36-0e3fca9864ac","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-216-18-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Col class=\u0022default-style\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:upper-alpha\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003EPersons engaged in road or street construction maintenance or repair, including but not limited to, employees of the City, and persons contracting to perform such work, may while engaged in the performance of that work, restrict the use of, and regulate the movement of traffic through or around the affected area whenever the traffic would endanger the safety of workers or the work would interfere with or endanger the movement of traffic through the area. Traffic may be regulated by warning signs, lights, appropriate control devices or by a person or persons controlling and directing the flow of traffic.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EIt is unlawful and an infraction for any person to disobey the instructions of a person controlling and directing traffic or to fail to comply with the directions of warning signs, lights or other control devices provided for the regulation of traffic pursuant to this section.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord 1413, \u00a7 1, 1987)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"125b8182-864e-45db-a54d-6315f3c629cc","prev_id":null}]}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f3824ea4-5ab9-4a5a-b19c-95af5461c964","ref":{"parent":"ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":1,"tag":"h3"},"pos":"212-217","docId":"75","text":"CHAPTER 11.37: OVERWEIGHT VEHICLE PERMIT","id":"f3824ea4-5ab9-4a5a-b19c-95af5461c964","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f3824ea4-5ab9-4a5a-b19c-95af5461c964\/de64c590-3e7b-4a40-a928-40f8f2389465","ref":{"parent":"f3824ea4-5ab9-4a5a-b19c-95af5461c964","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-217-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"de64c590-3e7b-4a40-a928-40f8f2389465","prev_id":null},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f3824ea4-5ab9-4a5a-b19c-95af5461c964\/67636f0f-0f85-4e8d-96b2-5d705e4d4e69","ref":{"parent":"f3824ea4-5ab9-4a5a-b19c-95af5461c964","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-217-12","docId":"75","text":"11.37.010 Purpose.","id":"67636f0f-0f85-4e8d-96b2-5d705e4d4e69","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f3824ea4-5ab9-4a5a-b19c-95af5461c964\/67636f0f-0f85-4e8d-96b2-5d705e4d4e69\/5a7514fc-7fa3-45b2-ac87-e30b3d8cf2c4","ref":{"parent":"67636f0f-0f85-4e8d-96b2-5d705e4d4e69","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-217-12-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EThe purpose of this chapter is to set forth the form and necessary fees for filing an application for a special permit authorizing the applicant to operate or move a vehicle or combination of vehicles of a size or weight or with a load exceeding the maximum as specified by the California Vehicle Code.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1538, \u00a7 1 (part), 1990)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"5a7514fc-7fa3-45b2-ac87-e30b3d8cf2c4","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f3824ea4-5ab9-4a5a-b19c-95af5461c964\/ea64a340-bb24-41db-8014-555129f3844a","ref":{"parent":"f3824ea4-5ab9-4a5a-b19c-95af5461c964","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-217-13","docId":"75","text":"11.37.020 Application.","id":"ea64a340-bb24-41db-8014-555129f3844a","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f3824ea4-5ab9-4a5a-b19c-95af5461c964\/ea64a340-bb24-41db-8014-555129f3844a\/c1dfbfc0-6a30-4de7-ac4d-26e3699a06ff","ref":{"parent":"ea64a340-bb24-41db-8014-555129f3844a","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-217-13-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EThis chapter shall apply to any vehicle which exceeds the size, weight and load allowances as set forth in California Vehicle Code Sections 35000 et seq.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1538, \u00a7 1 (part), 1990)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"c1dfbfc0-6a30-4de7-ac4d-26e3699a06ff","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f3824ea4-5ab9-4a5a-b19c-95af5461c964\/e4607528-fd65-45a5-b1b8-f62aa1227039","ref":{"parent":"f3824ea4-5ab9-4a5a-b19c-95af5461c964","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-217-14","docId":"75","text":"11.37.030 Form of Application for Special Permit.","id":"e4607528-fd65-45a5-b1b8-f62aa1227039","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f3824ea4-5ab9-4a5a-b19c-95af5461c964\/e4607528-fd65-45a5-b1b8-f62aa1227039\/c8758b90-b632-4c5c-b65e-1ce5f111c262","ref":{"parent":"e4607528-fd65-45a5-b1b8-f62aa1227039","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-217-14-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EAny applicant who is subject to this chapter and wishes a special permit authorizing the applicant to, with respect to streets and highways under Cupertino\u2019s jurisdiction, operate or move a vehicle or combination of vehicles or special mobile equipment of a size or weight of vehicle or load exceeding the maximum specified in California Vehicle Code Sections 35000 et seq., shall submit an application in the form as set forth in California Vehicle Code Section 35781, attached to the ordinance codified in this chapter as Exhibit A, which form application shall be available from the Cupertino Department of Public Works.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1538, \u00a7 1 (part), 1990)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"c8758b90-b632-4c5c-b65e-1ce5f111c262","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f3824ea4-5ab9-4a5a-b19c-95af5461c964\/9bd5dd2d-5ac8-472f-a95e-f20d3453b928","ref":{"parent":"f3824ea4-5ab9-4a5a-b19c-95af5461c964","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-217-15","docId":"75","text":"11.37.040 Fee for Processing Application.","id":"9bd5dd2d-5ac8-472f-a95e-f20d3453b928","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f3824ea4-5ab9-4a5a-b19c-95af5461c964\/9bd5dd2d-5ac8-472f-a95e-f20d3453b928\/b9a73add-3843-4510-8d9d-b69a4614242e","ref":{"parent":"9bd5dd2d-5ac8-472f-a95e-f20d3453b928","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-217-15-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Col class=\u0022default-style\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:upper-alpha\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe fees for processing and issuing a special permit pursuant to this chapter shall be as authorized by CVC Section 35795(b) \u201cand shall not exceed the fee schedule developed by the Department of Transportation.\u201d\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe charge per permit issued for repetitive loads of ten or more trips will be the same amount as is charged for the annual permit. To qualify as a repetitive load, the commodity must be of the same size and description, with evidence presented with the application of the anticipated number of loads and an estimate of the anticipated total time involved in the shipment. This type of permit shall also be limited to travel from the specified point of origin to the destination, i.e., restricted haul from point A to point B only. No charge shall be imposed on governmental agencies using their own equipment. Special services necessitated by unusually large or heavy loads requiring engineering investigations, escorts, tree trimming or other services shall be billed separately.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1629, 1993; Ord. 1538, \u00a7 1 (part), 1990)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"b9a73add-3843-4510-8d9d-b69a4614242e","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f3824ea4-5ab9-4a5a-b19c-95af5461c964\/0a187c47-546e-4d1c-b5d4-1f94a41b82fa","ref":{"parent":"f3824ea4-5ab9-4a5a-b19c-95af5461c964","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-217-16","docId":"75","text":"11.37.050 Issuance of Special Permit.","id":"0a187c47-546e-4d1c-b5d4-1f94a41b82fa","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f3824ea4-5ab9-4a5a-b19c-95af5461c964\/0a187c47-546e-4d1c-b5d4-1f94a41b82fa\/d3bb75c5-f8ac-428b-8b9d-45320ff08159","ref":{"parent":"0a187c47-546e-4d1c-b5d4-1f94a41b82fa","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-217-16-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EThe Director of Public Works may, at his or her discretion, upon the submittal of a complete application and if good cause appears, issue a special permit authorizing the applicant to operate or move a vehicle or combination of vehicles or special mobile equipment of a size and a weight of vehicle or load exceeding the maximum specified in California Vehicle Code Sections 35000 et seq.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1538, \u00a7 1 (part), 1990)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"d3bb75c5-f8ac-428b-8b9d-45320ff08159","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f3824ea4-5ab9-4a5a-b19c-95af5461c964\/c39dec4b-237b-4498-873e-43091a5cc215","ref":{"parent":"f3824ea4-5ab9-4a5a-b19c-95af5461c964","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-217-17","docId":"75","text":"11.37.060 Restrictions.","id":"c39dec4b-237b-4498-873e-43091a5cc215","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f3824ea4-5ab9-4a5a-b19c-95af5461c964\/c39dec4b-237b-4498-873e-43091a5cc215\/e98fad49-c737-46ee-9923-c093f5ebdc97","ref":{"parent":"c39dec4b-237b-4498-873e-43091a5cc215","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-217-17-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Cp\u003EThe Director of Public Works may withhold a special permit or, if the special permit is issued, limit the number of trips or establish seasonal or other time limitations within which the vehicle or vehicles described in this chapter may be operated, or otherwise limit or prescribe conditions of operation, when necessary to assure against undue damages to the road foundations, surfaces, structures, or roadside and overhead facilities, and may require an undertaking or other security necessary to protect the streets and highways from injury or to provide indemnity from any injury resulting from the operation of the vehicle.\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1538, \u00a7 1 (part), 1990)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"e98fad49-c737-46ee-9923-c093f5ebdc97","prev_id":null}]},{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f3824ea4-5ab9-4a5a-b19c-95af5461c964\/6f95280b-b4fa-4165-9b3d-729c10d7388b","ref":{"parent":"f3824ea4-5ab9-4a5a-b19c-95af5461c964","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"subsection","hasChildren":2,"tag":"h4"},"pos":"212-217-18","docId":"75","text":"11.37.070 Appeals.","id":"6f95280b-b4fa-4165-9b3d-729c10d7388b","children":[{"path":"\/ccb0cd02-0dd5-407b-bffd-162d19236255\/f3824ea4-5ab9-4a5a-b19c-95af5461c964\/6f95280b-b4fa-4165-9b3d-729c10d7388b\/e42da7ad-39c5-4761-b393-ad6a18a670d4","ref":{"parent":"6f95280b-b4fa-4165-9b3d-729c10d7388b","name":"subsection"},"li_attr":{"dataTag":"BodyM","hasChildren":0},"pos":"212-217-18-11","docId":"75","text":"\u003Col class=\u0022default-style\u0022 style=\u0022list-style-type:upper-alpha\u0022\u003E\u003Cli\u003EAny person aggrieved by a decision of the Director of Public Works under the provisions of this chapter may appeal such decision to the City Council by filing a written notice of the appeal with the City Clerk within five days after the date of the decision.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003ESaid notice of appeal must state:\u003Col\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe asserted error;\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe grounds upon which said appeal is taken; and\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe name and address of the party appealing. Said notice of appeal must be signed by the party appealing, or by his agent. Said notice of appeal shall not be effective unless it is filed with the City Clerk within the time required by subsection A of this section.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EA public hearing shall be held by the City Council within thirty days from the date of the filing of the notice.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003ENotice of the time and place of the hearing shall be given by mail, postage prepaid, and dispatched not less than ten days prior to the hearing to the applicant at his address as shown upon the notice of appeal.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EThe City Council shall hear the appeal. At the conclusion of the hearing, the Council may affirm, reverse or modify the action appealed; subject, however, to the provisions of this chapter. The findings and decisions of the City Council shall be entered upon the minutes of the City Council, and the decision shall be final and shall take effect as directed by the City Council.\u003C\/li\u003E\u003C\/ol\u003E\u003Cp\u003E(Ord. 1538, \u00a7 1 (part), 1990)\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E","id":"e42da7ad-39c5-4761-b393-ad6a18a670d4","prev_id":null}]}]}]}]